hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2401","71 - (2398) - And from Ibn Uyaynah, Amr reported to us, from Ata; and Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed it until as much of the night passed as Allah willed. So Umar said to him: O Messenger of Allah, the women and children have slept. So he came out and said: Were it not that I would burden my nation, I would pray it at this hour - meaning Isha."
"2402","72 - (2399) - And from Amr, he said: I heard Awsajah, freedman of Ibn Abbas, narrating from Ibn Abbas: that a man died in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) leaving no relative except a slave he had freed. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give him his inheritance."
"2403","73 - (2400) - And from Ibn Uyaynah, Ibrahim ibn Uqbah narrated to us, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas: that a woman brought out a boy from her litter and said: O Messenger of Allah, is there hajj for this one? He said: Yes, and you have reward."
"2404","74 - (2401) - Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eight and seven together. It was said to him: Why did he do that? He said: He intended not to burden his nation."
"2405","75 - (2402) - Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade breathing into a vessel or blowing into it."
"2406","76 - (2403) - Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The people used to leave in every direction, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should depart until his last contact is with the House."
"2407","77 - (2404) - Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Ahwal, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood to pray tahajjud at night, he said: O Allah, to You is praise; You are the Light of the heavens and the earth and who is in them. And to You is praise; You are the Sustainer of the heavens and the earth and who is in them. And to You is praise; You are the King of the heavens and the earth and who is in them. And to You is praise; You are the Truth, Your promise is true, meeting You is true, the Hour is true, Paradise is true, the Fire is true, and the prophets are true. O Allah, to You I submit, in You I believe, upon You I rely, to You I turn, by You I dispute, and to You I refer judgment. So forgive me what I did before and after, what I concealed and declared. You are the Advancer and the Delayer; there is no god but You, and there is no god besides You."
"2408","78 - (2405) - Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: We have no evil example: one who takes back his gift is like a dog returning to its vomit."
"2409","79 - (2406) - And from Ibn Uyaynah, from Asim, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank while standing."
"2410","80 - (2407) - And from Ibn Uyaynah, Ibn Abi Najih narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Kathir, from Abu al-Minhal, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah while they were advancing payment for dates - or fruits - for two and three years. So he said: Whoever advances payment for dates, let him advance for a known measure, a known time, to a known term."
"2411","81 - (2408) - Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Aban, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I asked Jibril: Which of the two terms did Musa fulfill? He said: The more complete and perfect of them."
"2412","82 - (2409) - Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Ahwal, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: What a Thursday! The day the pain of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intensified, so he said: Bring me, I will write for you a document after which you will not go astray. So they disputed - and disputing before a prophet is not proper. He said: Leave me, for what I am in is better than what you ask about. He said: He commanded them with three: he said: Expel the idolaters from the Arabian Peninsula, honor the delegations as I used to honor them, and the third - I do not know whether he said it and I forgot it, or he did not say it."
"2413","83 - (2410) - Abu Mamar Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Hudhali narrated to us, Jarir, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, Abdullah ibn Idris, Hafs ibn Ghiyath, Yahya ibn Sulaym and Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon you are white garments; let your living wear them, and shroud your dead in them. And upon you is antimony, for it clears the vision and grows the hair."
"2414","84 - (2411) - Abu Mamar narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Water is not made impure by anything."
"2415","85 - (2412) - Abu Mamar narrated to us, from Hushaym, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away when he was sixty-five years old."
"2416","86 - (2413) - Musab ibn Abdullah ibn Musab narrated to us, he said: al-Darawardi narrated to me, from Thawr ibn Zayd, from Ishaq ibn Jabir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who entices a slave against his master; he is not of us who corrupts a wife against her husband; and he is not of us who urges on horses on the day of racing."
"2417","87 - (2414) - Musab ibn Abdullah al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman and Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Abdullah ibn Ayyash Abu al-Mughirah, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade intercourse with pregnant women on the day of Khaybar; and: Do not water another's crop; and [he forbade] selling spoils before they are divided, eating the flesh of domestic donkeys, and every fanged beast of prey."
"2418","88 - (2415) - Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Mundhir, from Wahb, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Twelve thousand will come out from Aden aiding Allah and His Messenger; they are the best of those between me and them. Al-Mutamir said: I think he said: In the depths."
"2419","89 - (2416) - Abd al-Ala narrated to us, he said: al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to me, he said: I heard Layth, from Abu Fazarah, from Said ibn Jubayr, or Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, raising the hadith to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2420","90 - (2417) - And Mutamir said another time, from Abu Fazarah, from Miqsam, from Said, from Ibn Abbas, raising the hadith to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: These words are a cure for every disease: I seek refuge with the perfect words of Allah and all His names generally from the evil of the poisonous and the common, from the evil of the harmful eye, from the evil of the envier when he envies, and from the evil of Abu Qatarah and what he bore. Thirty-three angels came to their Lord and said: There is pain, pain in our land. So He said: Take from your earth and wipe your pain with the ruqyah of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Whoever takes a wage for it or conceals it from anyone will never prosper."
"2421","91 - (2418) - al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, Hiql narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Awzai, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank milk, then rinsed his mouth, then said: This has fat in it."
"2422","92 - (2419) - And from Hiql, he said: I heard al-Awzai, al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a dead sheep and said: Why did you not benefit from its skin? They said: O Messenger of Allah, it is dead. He said: Only eating it was forbidden."
"2423","93 - (2420) - Abu Salih narrated to us, Hiql narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Awzai, he said: Ata said: from Ibn Abbas: that a man suffered a wound in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then major impurity befell him, so he sought a ruling and was ruled to wash. So he washed and died. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: They killed him, may Allah kill them. Was not the cure for ignorance asking? 94 - (2421) - Ata said: It reached me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about that and said: Had he washed his body and left his head where the wound struck him, it would have sufficed him."
"2424","95 - (2422) - Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, he said: I heard Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying, and one of us wanted to pass in front of him, so he kept warding him off."
"2425","96 - (2423) - Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us, Shubah reported to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, he said: I heard Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I came with a boy from Banu Hashim on a donkey, and we passed in front of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying. So we dismounted from it, left the donkey eating from the greens of the earth - or he said: from the plants of the earth - and joined him in prayer. So a man said: Was there a short spear in front of him? He said: No."
"2426","97 - (2424) - Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) carried out mutual cursing between the two brothers of Banu Ajlan - or between a man and a woman; Abd al-Rahman doubted. He said: So her husband said: By Allah, I have not approached her since we watered after leaving [the palms dry] - and al-afr is watering the palms after leaving them without water after pollination by two months. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, make clear, make clear. He said: And the woman's husband had reddish-blond hair, thin forearms and shanks. He said: And the one with whom she was accused was Ibn al-Sahma. He said: So she gave birth to a black boy, curly, with tight curls, thick forearms, with thick shanks. So Ibn Shaddad said: O Abu al-Abbas, is she the woman about whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I stoned anyone without proof I would have stoned her? He said: So Ibn Abbas said: No. And he said: That was a woman who had openly [committed indecency] in Islam. Another man said: O Abu Abbas, how was the description? So Ibn Abbas said: She gave birth to him upon the bad description."
"2427","98 - (2425) - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahm narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave drink, he said: Begin with the elder - or he said: with the elders."
"2428","99 - (2426) - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahm narrated to us, Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed on the day of Tarwiyah at Mina the noon, afternoon, night and dawn prayers."
"2429","100 - (2427) - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahm narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak and Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Awf al-Arabi, from Ziyad ibn Husayn, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me on the morning of the pebbles: Bring me pebbles. So I picked for him pebbles of the size thrown between fingers. When he placed them in his hand he said: Yes, with the likes of these; yes, with the likes of these; yes, with the likes of these. And beware of excess in religion, for those before you were only destroyed by excess in religion."
"2430","101 - (2428) - Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad narrated to us, Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Five are killed by one in ihram: the kite, the mouse, the scorpion, the crow, and the vicious dog."
"2431","102 - (2429) - Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith reported to me that Bukayr narrated to him, from Kurayb, freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he entered the House, found in it a picture of Ibrahim and a picture of Maryam, and said: Yet they have heard that the angels do not enter a house in which there is a picture. This is Ibrahim depicted - what has he to do with divining arrows?"
"2432","103 - (2430) - Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Amr reported to me, from Abd Rabbih ibn Said, he said: al-Minhal ibn Amr narrated to me - and once he said: Said ibn Jubayr reported to me - from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited a sick person, he sat at his head, then said seven times: I ask Allah the Mighty, Lord of the Mighty Throne, to heal you. He said: If there was delay in his term, he was cured of that pain of his."
"2433","104 - (2431) - Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Razi reported to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to prostrate on seven limbs, and forbidden to gather a garment or hair."
"2434","105 - (2432) - And from Abu Jafar, from Abd al-Karim ibn Abi al-Mukhariq, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), about a man who had intercourse with his wife while menstruating, he said: If it was flowing blood, let him give a dinar in charity; and if there was yellowness in it, half a dinar."
"2435","106 - (2433) - Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abdullah al-Wasiti narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the effeminate among men and the masculine women. So I said: What are the masculine women? He said: Women resembling men."
"2436","107 - (2434) - Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Abi Thawr narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon every joint of a person is a prayer. So a man from the people said: This is hard; who can bear this? He said: Enjoining good and forbidding evil is a prayer; carrying for the weak is a prayer; and every step one of you takes toward prayer is a prayer."
"2437","108 - (2435) - Abu Mamar narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon every joint of the son of Adam each day is charity. Then he mentioned a similar hadith."
"2438","109 - (2436) - Abu Hammam narrated to us, Hammad ibn Usamah narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Zayd ibn al-Hawari, from Ibn Abbas, he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we go to our wives in Paradise as we go to them in this world? He said: By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, a man will go to a hundred virgins in a single morning."
"2439","110 - (2437) - Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Ali ibn Hashim ibn al-Barid narrated to us, from Mubarak ibn Hassan, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, which of our companions is best? He said: One whose seeing reminds you of Allah, whose speech increases your knowledge, and whose deed reminds you of the Hereafter."
"2440","111 - (2438) - Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A red cloak from what was taken from the idolaters was missing on the day of Badr. So some people said: Perhaps the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it? So Allah sent down: It is not for a prophet to embezzle. Khusayf said: So I said to Said: It is not for a prophet to embezzle. So he said: Rather he embezzles and kills too."
"2441","112 - (2439) - al-Hasan ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When Ali married Fatimah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give her something. He said: I have nothing. He said: Where is your Hutamiyyah coat of mail?"
"2442","113 - (2440) - And from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Azrah, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man saying the talbiyah on behalf of Shubrumah, so he said: O one saying talbiyah on behalf of Shubrumah, who is Shubrumah? He said: A brother of mine, or a relative of mine. He said: Did you perform hajj for yourself? He said: No. He said: Perform hajj for yourself, then perform hajj for Shubrumah."
"2443","114 - (2441) - Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Sukayn narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, he said: al-Fadl ibn Abbas was riding behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Arafah. The young man kept glancing at the women, looking at them, while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept turning his face away with his hand from behind, while the young man kept glancing at them. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Son of my brother, this is a day in which whoever controls his hearing, sight and tongue will be forgiven."
"2444","115 - (2442) - Abu Abd al-Rahman Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Allaf narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn al-Khattab ibn Ubaydullah ibn Abi Bakrah narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Abi Hafsah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Were it not that dogs are a community, I would have ordered killing every entirely black one. So kill the white-spotted among dogs, for they are the accursed of the jinn."
"2445","116 - (2443) - Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Kindi narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, freedman of the family of Talhah, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my sister vowed to perform hajj walking. So he said: Allah has no need of your sister's hardship in anything. Let her perform hajj riding and expiate her oath."
"2446","117 - (2444) - Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Ward, from al-Hasan ibn Habib, or Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two should not converse privately excluding a third, for that hurts him, and Allah dislikes harming a believer."
"2447","118 - (2445) - Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah and Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, they said: Ismail ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Nadr al-Khazzaz, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on Hira and the mountain shook. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be firm, Hira; there is upon you none but a prophet, or a truthful one, or a martyr. And upon it were the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar, Ali, Uthman, Talhah, al-Zubayr, Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, and Said ibn Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl."
"2448","And I wrote it from the hadith of Abu al-Rabi. 119 - (2446) - Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, Sharik ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abdullah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in a garment whose ends he crossed over each other, wrapping himself with it, shielding himself with the excess of the garment from the heat and cold of the ground."
"2449","120 - (2447) - Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, Sallam ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Abu Nadrah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated, he leveled himself, so that if water were poured on his back it would hold."
"2450","121 - (2448) - Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, Sallam ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrating on his garment."
"2451","122 - (2449) - Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, Hafs ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while fasting and in ihram, then he fainted. So he forbade the people that day from a fasting person being cupped, out of dislike of weakness upon him."
"2452","123 - (2450) - Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, Sallam ibn Salm al-Tawil narrated to us, from al-Fadl ibn Atiyyah, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sharp temper befalls the best of my nation."
"2453","124 - (2451) - Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave on the day of Badr to the horse two shares and to the man one share."
"2454","125 - (2452) - Hudbah narrated to us, Wahb narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, Ammar ibn Abi Ammar reported to us, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away when he was sixty-five years old. And al-Hasan used to say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away when he was sixty years old."
"2455","126 - (2453) - Abu Umar al-Harith ibn Surayj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Said ibn Jubayr, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Tamim al-Dari and Adiyy ibn Badda used to go to Makkah, and a man from Quraysh of Banu Sahm accompanied them. He died in a land where there was no Muslim, and entrusted his estate to them. When they arrived they delivered it to his family, concealing a silver cup inlaid with gold that was with him, saying: We did not see it. So they were brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who made them swear by Allah that they concealed nothing and came upon nothing, and let them go. Then the cup was found with some people of Makkah, who said: We bought it from Tamim al-Dari and Adiyy ibn Badda. So the heirs of the Sahmi stood, took the cup, and two men among them swore by Allah that this cup is our companion's cup, our testimony is more rightful than their testimony, and we did not transgress; indeed then we would be of the wrongdoers. And these two verses were sent down: O you who believe, testimony between you when death approaches one of you - to the end of the verse."
"2456","127 - (2454) - Harith ibn Surayj narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Abu Fazarah, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was not commanded to build lofty mosques. He said: And Ibn Abbas said: You will surely decorate them as the Jews and Christians decorated."
"2457","128 - (2455) - Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Qays, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that a woman from Khatham came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, I am an unmarried woman, and I wish to marry; so what is the husband's right upon his wife? If I am able to do it, otherwise I will remain unmarried? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The husband's right upon his wife is that when he desires her for himself while she is on the back of his camel, she does not refuse him. And among the husband's rights upon the wife is that she gives nothing from his house except with his permission; if she does that, the sin is upon her and the reward for another. And among the husband's rights upon the wife is that she does not leave his house except with his permission; if she does that, the angels curse her until she returns or repents."
"2458","129 - (2456) - And with it, he said: Ibn Abbas narrated to us, he said: When wind rose, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) faced it, knelt on his knees, and said: O Allah, make them winds, and do not make it wind. O Allah, make it mercy, and do not make it punishment."
"2459","130 - (2457) - Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, Husayn narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever takes an orphan among Muslims to his food and drink until Allah enriches him, Allah surely makes Paradise obligatory for him, unless he commits an unforgivable sin. And whoever raises three daughters, spends upon them and treats them well, Paradise becomes obligatory for him. So a bedouin man stood and said: Or two? He said: Yes, so that had he said one, he would have said: Yes. And there is no servant whose two precious things Allah takes away except his reward with Allah is in Paradise. He said: And what are his two precious things? He said: His two eyes. He said: And when Ibn Abbas narrated this hadith he said: By Allah, this is among the choicest and finest of hadith."
"2460","131 - (2458) - Wahb narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah gave every rightful one his right. And Allah prescribed obligations, established practices, set limits, permitted the lawful, forbade the unlawful, legislated Islam, and made it easy, tolerant and spacious, and did not make it narrow. O people, there is no faith for one with no trust, no religion for one with no covenant. Whoever breaks Allah's covenant, Allah will seek him; whoever breaks my covenant, I will dispute him; whoever I dispute, I overcome; whoever breaks my covenant will not attain my intercession nor come to me at the Pond. Verily Allah permitted killing only in three: an apostate after faith, an adulterer after chastity, or a killer of a soul, so he is killed for it. O Allah, have I conveyed?"
"2461","And from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed umrah, and between him and the people of Makkah was a pact that he would not take out anyone of its people. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) completed his umrah, he left Makkah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by the daughter of Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib. She said: O Messenger of Allah, to whom do you leave me? He did not heed the pact between him and the people of Makkah. Zayd ibn Harithah passed by her, and she said: To whom do you leave me? He did not heed her. Jafar passed by her, and she pleaded with him, but he did not heed her. Then Ali ibn Abi Talib passed by her, and she said: O Abu Hasan, to whom do you leave me? So Ali took her and placed her behind Fatimah. When they stopped, Zayd came to Ali and said: I have more right to her than you; I am the freedman of the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Ali said: I have more right to her than you. Jafar said: I have more right to her; her maternal aunt Asma bint Umays al-Khathamiyyah is with me. When their voices rose, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for them. When they came to him he said: As for you, O Jafar, you resemble my creation and character. And as for you, O Ali, I am from you and you are my successor. And as for Zayd, he is my freedman and yours. So hand the girl to her maternal aunt, for she has most right to her."
"2462","And from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Of ninety-nine women, one is in Paradise and the rest in the Fire. That was hard upon those of the Emigrants present with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a Muslim woman carries, she has the reward of one standing, fasting, in ihram, striving in the way of Allah, until when she delivers, then for the first suckling she nurses him she has the reward of giving life to a soul."
"2463","134 - (2461) - Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Thabit al-Abdi narrated to us, Jabalah ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in one of the houses of his wives, he placed his head on the thigh of one of them and dozed, then laughed in his sleep. After I saw him, some of the household asked him, saying: O Messenger of Allah, what made you laugh? So he said: I marveled at people of my nation riding this sea, facing the terror of the enemy, striving in the way. Then he mentioned to them a merit that Muhammad did not retain. A woman who was there said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah to make me among them. So he supplicated for her. Then a husband of hers went out with her in an expedition; while she was on the seashore riding her mount, she fell and her thigh broke, and she died."
"2464","135 - (2462) - Abd al-Ala ibn Jabir narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whomever you find having intercourse with an animal, kill him and kill the animal."
"2465","136 - (2463) - And from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whomever you find doing the deed of the people of Lut, kill the doer and the one done to."
"2466","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Wuhaib narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to prostrate on seven bones: the forehead, and he pointed with his hand to his nose, and the two hands, and the two knees, and the two feet, and not to tuck up the clothes nor the hair."
"2467","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Wuhaib narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from Ikrimah ibn Khalid, from Ibn Abbas, that he spent the night at his aunt Maymunah's house, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood up at night and prayed. He said: So I stood to his left, and he pulled me until he placed me on his right. He said: Then he prayed thirteen rak'ahs, his standing in them being equal."
"2468","Al-Hasan ibn Umar ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, al-Aswad ibn Hafs al-Marwazi narrated to us, Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, from Yazid al-Nahwi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he returned from a journey, would kiss his daughter Fatimah."
"2469","Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab saw a gold ring on my hand, so he took it and threw it away, and said — then I neither sought it nor did he return it to me."
"2470","Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Zayd, from al-Qa'qa' ibn Hakim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Wa'lah, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas about selling wine to the dhimmis, and he said: A man from Thaqif or from Daws gave as a gift to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a waterskin of wine in the year of the Conquest, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had been his friend in the pre-Islamic period. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Allah has indeed forbidden it. Then he whispered to a servant boy with him, saying: Go with it to al-Hazwarah — a village beside Madinah — and sell it. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What did you order him? He said: I ordered him to sell it. He said: O so-and-so, indeed the One who forbade drinking it has forbidden its price. So he ordered that it be poured out."
"2471","Abu Hisham al-Rifa'i narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Rushdayn ibn Kurayb narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the evil of what the wind brings, and from the evil of what the messengers bring."
"2472","Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Husayn ibn Abdullah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a rainy day shielding himself with a cloak, with mud on him when he prostrated."
"2473","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while he was fasting and in ihram."
"2474","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about one who shaved before slaughtering and the like, and he would say: No harm, no harm."
"2475","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Husayn, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Bring me pebbles. He said: So I picked up for him pebbles that were the pebbles for stoning, and when I placed them in his hand he said: Yes, with the likes of these. And beware of extremism in religion, for those before you were destroyed only by extremism in religion."
"2476","And from Hushaym, Abu Bishr narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: that a man was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in ihram, when his she-camel threw him off and he died. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wash him with water and lote leaves, and shroud him in two garments, for he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah."
"2477","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived pronouncing ihram for Hajj; he performed tawaf and sa'y and did not exit ihram because of the sacrificial animal, and he ordered whoever did not have a sacrificial animal with him to perform tawaf and sa'y and shorten or shave, then exit ihram."
"2478","And from Hushaym, Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would continue reciting the talbiyah for Umrah until he touched the Black Stone."
"2479","And from Hushaym, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive those who shave. A man said: And those who shorten. So he said: O Allah, forgive those who shave. He said on the third or fourth time: And those who shorten."
"2480","And from Hushaym, Khalid narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped my head and prayed for me for wisdom."
"2481","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Ikrimah, he said: I saw a man at the Maqam saying takbir at every rising and lowering, so I met Ibn Abbas and said: I saw a man saying takbir at every rising and lowering. He said: Is that not the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? May Ikrimah have no mother?"
"2482","And from Hushaym, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the offspring of the polytheists, and he said: Allah knows best what they would have done."
"2483","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Khabbab, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr ibn Abd al-Muttalib came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I want to perform Hajj; should I stipulate? He said: Yes, stipulate. She said: How should I say? He said: Say: Labbayk, O Allah, labbayk; my place of exiting ihram is wherever You detain me."
"2484","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abbad narrated to us, al-Hajjaj informed us, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proposed to Maymunah, and she entrusted her affair to al-Abbas, so he married her to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2485","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah and Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, they said: Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Ya'qub ibn Utbah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) confirmed Umayyah ibn Abi al-Salt in two verses of his poetry. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He spoke the truth."
"2486","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Minhal, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever visits a sick person whose death has not yet come and says: I ask Allah the Mighty, Lord of the Mighty Throne, to heal you — seven times — he will be healed."
"2487","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Hafs narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote a document between the Muhajirun and the Ansar: that they should not neglect their blood-money obligations, and that they should ransom their captives with kindness and reconciliation between people."
"2488","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Aththam ibn Ali narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Habib, from Sa'id, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray two rak'ahs then use the siwak."
"2489","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed wudu: he scooped a handful and washed his face, then scooped a handful and washed his right hand, then scooped a handful and washed his left hand, then scooped a handful and wiped his head and his ears, inserting his index fingers inside them and passing his thumbs over the outer part of his ears, wiping their outer and inner sides, then scooped a handful and washed his right foot, then scooped a handful and washed his left foot."
"2490","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no wudu upon one who sleeps while prostrating until he lies down, for when he lies down his joints relax."
"2491","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Ruzayq, from Abdullah ibn Isa, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: While Jibril was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he heard a sound from above him, so he raised his head and said to him: A door of heaven has been opened that was never opened before. Then an angel came to him and said: Receive glad tidings of two lights you have been given that no prophet before you was given: the Opening of the Book and the closing verses of Surat al-Baqarah; you will not recite a letter from them except that you will be given it."
"2492","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Mus'ab ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, from Mindal, from Ibn Jurayj, from Umar ibn Ata, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A servant girl belonging to the family of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) committed adultery, so he said: O Ali, apply the hadd to her. He said: So he left her until she delivered what was in her womb, then he struck her fifty lashes, then he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that. He said: You did right."
"2493","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would deliver the Friday sermon standing, then sit, then stand and deliver."
"2494","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he forbade eating every predator with fangs, and killing children, and selling the spoils before division, and — I think he said — approaching pregnant captives."
"2495","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) trotted in his Hajj and his Umrah, as did Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, and the caliphs after."
"2496","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abu Hadir, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Sacrificial camels became scarce in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he ordered the people to use cows."
"2497","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Ibn Abi Najih, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never fought a people until he had invited them."
"2498","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Numayr and Abd al-A'la narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The price of a shield in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was ten dirhams."
"2499","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Ismail, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking from the mouth of the bent vessel."
"2500","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade confining a living soul as a target. He said: And al-Zuhri said: Castration is a severe form of confinement."
"2501","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ya'la narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ghaylan narrated to us, from Layth, from Ata, Tawus and Mujahid, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he and his Companions, performed only one tawaf for their Umrah and their Hajj."
"2502","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ya'la narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, Ghaylan narrated to us, from Uthman Abu al-Yaqzan, from Ja'far ibn Iyas, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When this verse was revealed: And those who hoard gold and silver — he said: That weighed heavily on the Muslims, and they said: None of us can leave wealth for his child after him. So Umar said: I will relieve you. They went, and Umar went, and Thawban followed him, and he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, this verse has weighed heavily on your Companions. So the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah did not impose zakat except to purify what remains of your wealth, and He only prescribed inheritances in wealth so that it remains for those after you. He said: So Umar said takbir. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Shall I not tell you what a man hoards? The righteous woman; when he looks at her she pleases him, and when he commands her she obeys him, and when he is absent from her she guards him."
"2503","Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Rukanah, the brother of Banu Abd al-Muttalib, divorced the daughter of Abd Yazid in one sitting three times, and grieved over her intensely. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: How many times did you divorce her, O Rukanah? He said: Three times in one sitting. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then it is one."
"2504","Masruq ibn al-Marzuban narrated to us, Ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Quraysh said to the Jews: Give us something to ask this man about. So they said: Ask him about the soul. So they asked him, and it was revealed: And they ask you about the soul; say, the soul is from the command of my Lord, and you have not been given of knowledge except a little. They said: We have not been given of knowledge except a little, yet we have been given the Torah, and whoever is given the Torah has been given much good. So it was revealed: Say, if the sea were ink for the words of my Lord — the verse."
"2505","Masruq ibn al-Marzuban al-Kufi narrated to us, Ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Ibn Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The devils had seats in which they listened to the revelation; when they heard a word they added nine to it. The word itself would be true, while what they added would be false. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sent, they were barred from their seats, so they complained of that to Iblis — and the stars had not been used as missiles before that — so he said: This must be for a matter that has occurred on earth. Strike out across the earth. So they set out and found the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) between the two mountains of Nakhlah praying, and they came to him and reported, and he said: This is the event that has occurred on earth."
"2506","Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you eats, let him not wipe his hand until he licks it or has it licked."
"2507","Hannad ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Matar ibn Maymun al-Muharibi narrated to me, he said: Ikrimah narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a man from his Companions to a Jewish man and ordered him to kill him. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I cannot do that unless you permit me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: War is deception, so do what you wish."
"2508","Ismail ibn Musa narrated to us, Husayn ibn Isa narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Hazim, from Ibn Abbas, he said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at al-Hudaybiyah, he said: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; the help of Allah and the victory have come, and the people of Yemen have come. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what are the people of Yemen? He said: A people whose hearts are tender and whose natures are gentle; faith is Yemeni, understanding is Yemeni, and wisdom is Yemeni."
"2509","Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, and Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A morning or evening expedition in the path of Allah is better than the world and what is in it."
"2510","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from A'ishah, and from Hajjaj, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no marriage except with a guardian. And in the hadith of Urwah: And the ruler is the guardian of one who has no guardian."
"2511","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Qutbah ibn Abd al-Aziz, from al-A'mash, from Abu Yahya al-Qattat, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade inciting animals against one another."
"2512","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Sharik, from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade inciting animals against one another."
"2513","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Sayf ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn Sa'd narrated to me, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged with an oath and a witness."
"2514","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abd al-Salam narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram at the end of the prayer."
"2515","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abu Khalid narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, from Khusayf, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: I mentioned to Ibn Abbas the ihram of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made ihram obligatory when he finished his prayer, then he went out, and when he mounted his she-camel and it stood upright with him, he recited the talbiyah. Some people witnessed that from him and said: He recited the talbiyah when his she-camel stood up with him, for they witnessed only that. Then he traveled until he ascended al-Bayda and recited the talbiyah, and men with him witnessed, and they said: He recited the talbiyah when he ascended al-Bayda."
"2516","Dawud ibn Amr ibn Zuhayr al-Dabbi narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Zinad Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from his father, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) carried out li'an between al-Ajlani and his wife. Her husband said that day: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I have not approached her since we trod the dusty ground. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept saying that day: O Allah, make clear. The woman's husband was a man with reddish hair and thin forearms and shins, and the one she was accused with was the son of a black woman. Then she gave birth to a black boy with curly tight hair, thick forearms and fleshy shins. A man said to him: O Abu Abbas, how did you say? He said: I said: She gave birth to him upon the evil description. Then Ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had said to him: Is she the one about whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If I were to stone without evidence? He said: No, that was a woman who had openly committed indecency in Islam."
"2517","Dawud ibn Amr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother died without making a will; will it benefit her if I give charity on her behalf? He said: Yes."
"2518","Dawud ibn Amr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu Ma'bad, the freedman of Ibn Abbas, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivered a sermon and said: No woman should travel except with a mahram with her. He said: Then a man stood and said: I have been enrolled for battle, and I wanted to perform Hajj with my wife. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform Hajj with your wife."
"2519","Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I passed on the night I was taken by night in a pleasant scent, and I said: What is this scent, O Jibril? He said: This is the hairdresser of Pharaoh's daughter. She was combing her when the comb fell from her hand, and she said: In the name of Allah. Pharaoh's daughter said: My father? She said: My Lord and your father's Lord. She said: Shall I tell him then? She said: Tell him. He said to her: Do you have a lord other than me? She said: My Lord and your Lord, who is in heaven. He said: Then a cow of copper was heated for her. She said: I have a request to you. He said: What is your request? She said: That you gather my bones and the bones of my child. He said: That is yours upon us for the right you have upon us. So he threw her children into the cow one by one, the last of them being an infant boy, who said to her: O my mother, be patient, for you are upon the truth. Ibn Abbas said: Four spoke while they were infants: the son of the hairdresser of Pharaoh's daughter, the infant of Jurayj, Isa son of Maryam, and the fourth I do not remember."
"2520","Abu Hammam narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Khaythamah, from Ismail al-Suddi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that a lahd grave was dug for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2521","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Mu'ammal, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When people differ, the truth is with Mudar, and when Rabi'ah becomes mighty, that is the humiliation of Islam."
"2522","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Ismail, from Dawud ibn Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A neighbor may place his timber on his neighbor's wall even if he dislikes it, and the thoroughfare road is seven cubits, and there is no harm nor reciprocal harm."
"2523","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Kurayb, from Kurayb, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cursed is one who diminishes anything of the boundaries of the earth without right."
"2524","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abu Khalid narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: He is not of us who approaches a pregnant woman."
"2525","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Sinan, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over a dead person after he was buried."
"2526","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Abi Ghaniyyah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Isa, from al-Hasan, he said: Ibn Abbas informed me that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: O Allah, I have made Madinah sacred just as Makkah was made sacred."
"2527","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that a woman accepted Islam in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then her husband came after her and said: O Messenger of Allah, she had accepted Islam with me. So he returned her to him."
"2528","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that an unmarried virgin girl came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that her father had married her off while she was unwilling, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave her the choice."
"2529","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ya'la narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasted until he reached Usfan, then broke his fast."
"2530","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Abu Salih, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed on the day of Hunayn three shares to the horseman and one share to the foot soldier."
"2531","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I sighted the crescent tonight. He said: Do you bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger? He said: Yes. He said: Stand, O Bilal, and announce among the people that they should fast tomorrow."
"2532","Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Azrah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the dawn prayer on Friday: Alif Lam Mim, the Revelation, and Has there come upon man."
"2533","Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Imran ibn Hudayr informed me, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, that Ibn Abbas delayed the Maghrib prayer one night, so a man said to him: The prayer. He remained silent. Then he said to him: The prayer. So he said to him: May you have no mother, do you teach us about the prayer? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sometimes combine the two in Madinah."
"2534","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah and Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever changes his religion, kill him."
"2535","Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that Ali was brought people from the Zutt whom they found worshipping an idol, so he burned them. That reached Ibn Abbas, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only said: Whoever changes his religion, kill him."
"2536","Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise."
"2537","Abu Ibrahim al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: I heard Ibn Bukayr narrating, he said: Al-Layth narrated to me, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from Ibn Shihab, he said: Ibn Hazm narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas and Abu Habbah al-Ansari, they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When I was taken by night, I appeared at a level where I heard the scratching of the pens."
"2538","Ubaydullah ibn Umar ibn Maysarah narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Nahik, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever asks you by the face of Allah, give him; and whoever seeks refuge with you in Allah, grant him refuge."
"2539","Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn al-Akhnas narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Mulaykah narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As if I am looking at him, black and bow-legged, tearing it down stone by stone — meaning the Ka'bah."
"2540","Al-Qawariri Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Abd al-A'la ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qays ibn Sa'd, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he raised his head from bowing, would say: O Allah, our Lord, to You is praise filling the heavens and filling the earth, and filling whatever You will after that."
"2541","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zuhayr ibn Muhammad, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah has cursed one who slaughters for other than Allah, and Allah has cursed one who changes the boundaries of the earth, and Allah has cursed one who leads the blind astray from the path, and Allah has cursed one who curses his parents, and Allah has cursed one who takes others than his patrons as patrons, and Allah has cursed one who does the deed of the people of Lut — he said it three times — meaning the people of Lut."
"2542","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever claims affiliation to other than his father, or takes others than his patrons as patrons, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people."
"2543","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Aban al-Attar narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Aliyah al-Riyahi, from the cousin of your Prophet, Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate with these at distress: There is no god but Allah, the Mighty, the Forbearing; there is no god but Allah, Lord of the Mighty Throne; there is no god but Allah, Lord of the seven heavens and Lord of the Mighty Throne."
"2544","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, from Rafi' Abu al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon the valley of al-Azraq and said: What is this valley? It was said: The valley of al-Azraq. He said: As if I am looking at Musa descending, with loud crying to his Lord in talbiyah. And he passed by the pass of Kada', and said: What is this? He said: The pass of Kada'. He said: As if I am looking at Yunus ibn Matta upon a curly-haired red she-camel whose bridle is of fiber, wearing a woolen cloak."
"2545","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us, and we gave him to drink from this nabidh — meaning the nabidh of the water service — and he drank, then said: You have done well; do like this."
"2546","Abu Ya'la narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is none from the children of Adam except that he has erred or intended an error, except Yahya ibn Zakariyya. And it is not fitting for anyone to say: I am better than Yunus ibn Matta."
"2547","Zuhayr narrated to us, Shabbabah ibn Sawwar narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas, from his father, he said: Al-Abbas said to me: Spend the night with the family of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and observe the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he instructed me not to sleep until I had observed the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Isha and left the mosque until none remained in it but me. He said: Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at me and said: Who is this, Abdullah? He said: I said: Yes. He said: What is the matter with you? He said: I said: Al-Abbas ordered me to spend this night with you. He said: Then go ahead. He said: Spread it out, Abdullah. He said: So I brought a cushion of sackcloth stuffed with fiber. He said: Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stepped forward and prayed two rak'ahs, neither long nor short, then came to his bed until I heard his snoring, then he woke and recited: Indeed in the creation of the heavens and the earth and the alternation of night and day — until he completed the surah. Then he wiped three times, then stood and urinated, then cleaned his teeth with the siwak, then performed wudu, then stood and prayed two rak'ahs, neither long nor short, then returned to his bed and slept until I heard his snoring. Then he woke, then sat up on his bed, and did as he had done the first time, then wiped three times, and recited the verses from the end of Surah Al Imran: Indeed in the creation of the heavens and the earth and the alternation of night and day — until he completed the surah. Then he stood and cleaned his teeth with the siwak, then performed wudu, then prayed two rak'ahs, neither long nor short, then returned to his bed and slept until I heard his snoring. Then he woke and did as he had done the first two times: he prayed six rak'ahs, then prayed witr with three, then prayed the two rak'ahs before Fajr. When he finished his prayer he said: O Allah, place light in my sight, and light in my hearing, and light in my heart, and light before me, and light behind me, and light above me, and light beneath me, and light on my right, and light on my left, and appoint for me light on the Day of Resurrection, and magnify light for me."
"2548","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Nafi' narrated to us, from Wahb ibn Minas al-Adani, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he intended the prostration after the rak'ah, would say: O Allah, to You is praise filling the heavens and filling the earth and filling whatever You will after that."
"2549","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Yahya, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man's thigh exposed, and said: Cover your thigh, for a man's thigh is his awrah."
"2550","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Suhayb al-Basri, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying when two slave girls from Quraysh came and took hold of his knees — I think he said: so he separated between them — and prayed. And I came with a boy from Banu Hashim upon a donkey, and we passed in front of him, then we joined the prayer, and he did not turn away."
"2551","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Ismail narrated to me, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that when he dispatched his armies he would say: Go out in the name of Allah; fight in the path of Allah those who disbelieve in Allah. Do not betray, do not mutilate, do not steal from the spoils, do not kill children, nor the occupants of monasteries."
"2552","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Abu Ja'far and al-Zuhri, from Yazid ibn Hurmuz, he said: Najdah al-Haruri wrote to Ibn Abbas asking him about the share of the near relatives, to whom does it belong? And about killing children, mentioning in his letter that the learned companion of Musa had killed the boy. And about women, did they attend war with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? And did he assign them a share? Yazid said: So I wrote Ibn Abbas's letter for him, and he wrote to him: You wrote asking me about the share of the near relatives, to whom does it belong? It belongs to us, the People of the House. Umar ibn al-Khattab had invited us to marry off our unmarried from it, and provide servants for our poor from it, and pay the debts of our debtors from it, but we refused except that he hand it over to us, and he refused that, so we left it. And you wrote asking me about killing children, mentioning that the learned companion of Musa killed the boy. If you knew of children what that learned man knew, you would kill, but you do not know, so avoid them, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade killing them. And you wrote asking me about women, did they attend war with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? And did he assign them a share? They did attend with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but as for assigning them a share, no; he would give them a small gift. Muhammad said: One whom I do not suspect narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Hurmuz, that in his letter he asked him about slaves, did they attend war with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? And did he assign them a share? And about the orphan, when does he leave orphanhood and his right in the fay occur? So he wrote to him: Slaves did attend war with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but as for assigning them a share, no; he would give them a small gift. As for the orphan, when he reaches puberty he leaves orphanhood and his right in the fay occurs."
"2553","Zuhayr narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the most generous of people, and he was most generous in Ramadan when Jibril met him. He would meet him every night in Ramadan and revise the Qur'an with him. When Jibril met him, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was more generous than the blowing wind."
"2554","Zuhayr narrated to us, Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Warqa ibn Umar al-Yashkuri narrated to us, he said: I heard Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid narrating from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to relieve himself, so I placed wudu water for him. When he came out he said: Who placed this? They said: Ibn Abbas. He said: O Allah, give him understanding."
"2555","Zuhayr narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to let his hair hang down. The polytheists used to part their heads, and the People of the Book used to let their hair hang down. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to love agreeing with the People of the Book in what had not been revealed to him, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) parted his head."
"2556","Zuhayr narrated to us, Shabbabah ibn Sawwar narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray witr with three: Glorify the name of your Lord the Most High, and Say, O disbelievers, and Say, He is Allah, One."
"2557","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Qays ibn al-Hajjaj, from Hanash al-San'ani, from Abdullah ibn Abbas, that he narrated that he rode behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O boy, I am teaching you words: Guard Allah and He will guard you; guard Allah and you will find Him before you. When you ask, ask Allah; when you seek help, seek help from Allah. And know that if the nation gathered to benefit you with something, they would not benefit you except with something Allah has written for you; and if they gathered to harm you, they would not harm you except with something Allah has written against you. The pens have been lifted and the pages have dried."
"2558","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Thawr ibn Zayd, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that he said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and pledged allegiance to him in the mosque, then left. Then he stood and spread his legs and urinated. The people rushed at him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not interrupt the man's urination. Then he called him and said: Are you not a Muslim? He said: Yes. He said: What carried you to urinate in the mosque? He said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I thought it was only a level ground among grounds, so I urinated in it. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a bucket of water, and it was poured over his urine."
"2559","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Tawus al-Yamani, he said: I said to Abdullah ibn Abbas: They claim that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bathe on Friday, and wash your heads unless you are in major impurity, and touch perfume. So Ibn Abbas said: As for perfume, I do not know; as for bathing, yes."
"2560","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Abu Jamrah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray at night after Isha thirteen rak'ahs."
"2561","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Arqam ibn Shurahbil, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died without making a will."
"2562","Zuhayr narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Malik al-Muzani narrated to us, from Hanzalah ibn Abdullah al-Sadusi, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed two rak'ahs in which he recited only the Mother of the Book, adding nothing to it."
"2563","Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Zibyan, he said: Ibn Abbas said: Which of the two readings do you count as the first reading? They said: The reading of Abdullah. He said: Our reading is the first reading, and the reading of Abdullah is the last reading. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would have the Qur'an presented to him every Ramadan once; in the year in which he died it was presented to him twice, so Abdullah witnessed it, and witnessed what was abrogated of it and what was altered."
"2564","Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Mas'ud ibn Malik, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was aided by the east wind, and Ad were destroyed by the west wind."
"2565","Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khazim Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Hajjaj ibn Artah, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed on the day of Ta'if whoever came out to him from the slaves of the polytheists."
"2566","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hammam ibn Yahya informed us, Ata narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw a canopy dripping clarified butter and honey, and the people took from it — some taking much of it, some taking little, and some in between — and as if a rope was let down from heaven, then you came and took hold of it and rose, and Allah raised you. Then a man came after you and took hold of it and rose, and Allah raised him. Then a man came after you two and took hold of it and rose. Then a man came after you all and took hold of it, then it was cut off with him, then it was joined for him, and he rose, and Allah raised him. So Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, permit me to interpret it. He permitted him, and he said: As for the canopy, it is Islam; as for the clarified butter and honey, it is the Qur'an; as for the rope, it is what you are upon — you rise and Allah raises you. Then there will be a man after you upon your way, and he will rise and Allah will raise him. Then there will be a man after you two taking your way, and he will rise and Allah will raise him. Then there will be a man after you all upon your way, then it will be cut off with him, then joined for him, and he will rise and Allah will raise him. He said: Did I get it right, O Messenger of Allah? He said: You got some right and missed some. He said: I swear, O Messenger of Allah, you will tell me. He said: Do not swear."
"2567","Zuhayr narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Sayf ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never circumambulated anything except that it was part of the House."
"2568","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah and saw the Jews fasting Ashura, he said: What is this day that you fast? They said: This is a righteous day; this is a day in which Allah saved the Children of Isra'il from their enemy. He said: Then Musa fasted it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have more right to Musa than you. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasted it and ordered fasting it."
"2569","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slaughtered then shaved."
"2570","Zuhayr narrated to us, Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Avoid drinking from gourds, green jars, and pitch-coated vessels. Drink from waterskins; if you dislike their sourness, dilute it with water."
"2571","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ahwas ibn Jawwab al-Dabbi narrated to us, Ammar ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Sumay' the freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I stood with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in prayer on his left, so he took my hand and placed me on his right."
"2572","Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Fitr, from Shurahbil ibn Sa'd, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim who has two daughters and treats them well as long as they accompany him, or he accompanies them, except that they will admit him into Paradise."
"2573","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Dawud narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Sa'igh, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the Fitr prayer with the people, two rak'ahs without adhan, and delivered a sermon after the prayer. Then he took Bilal's hand and went to the women and addressed them, then ordered Bilal after he turned away from them to come to them and command them to give charity."
"2574","Zuhayr narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: I heard Ata say: I heard Ibn Abbas say: I heard the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: If the son of Adam had a valley full of wealth, he would love to have another like it. Nothing fills the soul of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah turns to whoever repents. Ibn Abbas said: I do not know whether it is from the Qur'an or not."
"2575","Zuhayr narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions performed Umrah from al-Ji'ranah, trotting around the House three times and walking four."
"2576","Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki' ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, Salih ibn Rustum narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The prayer was established and I had not prayed the two rak'ahs, so he saw me praying them, passed by me and said: Do you want to pray Fajr as four? It was said to Ibn Abbas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes."
"2577","Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abdullah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in a cloak, shielding himself with its excess from the heat and cold of the ground."
"2578","Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Yusuf al-Azraq narrated to us, from Awf al-A'rabi, from Sa'id ibn Abi al-Hasan, he said: I was with Ibn Abbas when a man came to him and said: I am a man whose livelihood is only from the work of my hand, and I make these images. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever makes an image, Allah will punish him on the Day of Resurrection until he breathes the soul into it, and he will never breathe into it. He said: The man trembled violently and his face turned pale. So Ibn Abbas said: Woe to you, if you must make, then upon you is this tree and everything in which there is no soul."
"2579","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Mughirah ibn al-Nu'man, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among the people and exhorted them, saying: O people, you will be gathered to Allah barefoot, naked, uncircumcised. Then he recited: As We began the first creation, We will repeat it — a promise upon Us; indeed We will do it. He said: And men will be brought and taken to the left, so I will say as the righteous servant said: And I was a witness over them as long as I was among them; when You took me, You were the Watcher over them, and You are Witness over all things. If You punish them, they are Your servants; if You forgive them, You are the Mighty, the Wise. He said: Then it will be said to me: They have continued turning back on their heels since you left them. He said: And the first to be clothed will be Ibrahim, peace be upon him."
"2580","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Husayn ibn Abdullah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the dyed garment for the muhrim as long as there is no scattering of dye or red mark."
"2581","Zuhayr narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ma'iz: Is what reached me about you true? He said: What reached you about me? He said: It reached me that you fell upon the slave girl of Banu so-and-so. He said: Yes. So he testified four testimonies, and he ordered that he be stoned."
"2582","Zuhayr narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) speaking clear speech, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed, some eloquence is magic, and indeed, some poetry is wisdom."
"2583","Zuhayr narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no omen, no contagion, no hama, no safar. A man said to him: O Messenger of Allah, we take the mangy sheep and cast it among the flock and it infects them. He said: Then who infected the first?"
"2584","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Yahya ibn so-and-so, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Abu Talib fell ill, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to visit him, and at his head was the seat of a man. Abu Jahl stood and sat in it. They complained to Abu Talib about him, saying: He attacks our gods. He said: O son of my brother, what do you want with this? He said: O uncle, I only want them to utter a word by which the Arabs will submit to them and the non-Arabs will pay them jizyah. He said: What is it? He said: There is no god but Allah. He said: Has he made the gods one god? This is a wondrous thing."
"2585","Zuhayr narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Ya'la ibn Hakim narrating from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out in the illness in which he died with his head bound in a cloth, sat upon the pulpit, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: There is none among people more generous to me with himself and his wealth than the son of Abu Quhafah. If I were to take a close friend from people, I would take Abu Bakr, but the brotherhood of Islam is better. Close every small door into the mosque except the small door of Abu Bakr."
"2586","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-A'la, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is asked about knowledge and conceals it will come on the Day of Resurrection bridled with a bridle of fire; and whoever speaks about the Qur'an without knowledge will come on the Day of Resurrection bridled with a bridle of fire."
"2587","Zuhayr narrated to us, Hashim narrated to us, Imran ibn Zayd al-Taghlibi narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Tamim narrated to me, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Abdullah ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There will be in the end of time a people nicknamed al-Rafidah; they reject Islam and cast it off, so kill them, for they are polytheists."
"2588","Zuhayr narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Yunus ibn Yazid al-Ayli narrating from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The best of companions are four, the best of detachments are four hundred, the best of armies are four thousand, and twelve thousand will never be defeated due to fewness."
"2589","Zuhayr narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man went out from Khaybar, followed by two men, with another following them, saying: Go back, go back — until he turned them back. Then he caught up with the first and said: These two are devils, and I kept with them until I turned them back. When you come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), convey peace to him and inform him that we are here gathering our charities; had they been suitable we would have sent them to him. He said: When the man arrived at Madinah, he informed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and thereupon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade seclusion."
"2590","Hashim ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, with its chain, similar to it."
"2591","Zuhayr narrated to us, Rib'i ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from Ibn Wa'lah, from Ibn Abbas, that a man went out while wine was lawful, and gave as a gift to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a waterskin of wine. He came with it led upon a camel until he found the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sitting, and said: What is this with you? He said: A waterskin of wine I gifted to you. He said: Did you know that Allah has forbidden it? He said: No. He said: Allah has indeed forbidden it. He said: Then the man turned to the camel driver and spoke to him something between him and him. He said: What did you say to him? He said: I ordered him to sell it. He said: The One who forbade drinking it has forbidden selling it. He said: Then he ordered the mouth of the waterskin opened, and it was poured out and flowed into the dust. I looked at it in the plain with nothing in it."
"2592","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Sufyan informed us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never fought a people until he had invited them."
"2593","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibrahim Abu Ishaq narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Hind, Thawr narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would glance in his prayer right and left, without turning his neck."
"2594","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Mus'ab narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a dead sheep its owners had discarded, and said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, the world is more insignificant to Allah than this is to its owners."
"2595","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hammam ibn Yahya informed us, Ata narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the Ka'bah, in which were six pillars, and stood at each pillar without praying."
"2596","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Nafi' ibn Umar, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, he said: Ibn Abbas wrote to me: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If people were given by their claims, people would claim the blood and wealth of people. But the oath is upon the defendant."
"2597","Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent his women ahead on the night of Muzdalifah before the crowding."
"2598","Zuhayr narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Amir narrated to us, from Hammam, from Ata, that Ibn al-Zubayr prayed Maghrib and gave salam after two rak'ahs, then stood to touch the Corner, so the people glorified Allah to him, and he returned and prayed a rak'ah. He said: So I came to Ibn Abbas and informed him of that, and he said: He did not deviate from the sunnah of his Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2599","Zuhayr narrated to us, Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The righteous dream is one seventieth part of prophethood."
"2600","Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — Jarir and others said: He did not raise it — he said: Circumambulation of the House is like prayer, except that you speak in it; whoever speaks in it, let him speak only good."
"2601","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Jabbar al-Khattabi narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Qays ibn Habtar, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The price of a dog is foul. And he said: If he comes to you seeking the price of the dog, fill his palm with dust."
"2602","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in an open space with nothing before him."
"2603","Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: I asked Sa'id ibn Jubayr about fasting Rajab — what do you think of it? He said: Ibn Abbas narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would fast until we said: He will not break fast, and break fast until we said: He will not fast."
"2604","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ja'far al-Raqqi narrated to us, Ubaydullah — meaning Ibn Amr — narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A people will dye with black at the end of time, like the crops of pigeons; they will not smell the scent of Paradise."
"2605","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: Abu Jahl said: If I see Muhammad praying at the Ka'bah, I will come to him until I tread upon his neck. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had he done so, the angels would have seized him openly. Had the Jews wished for death, they would have died and seen their seats in the Fire. Had those who would imprecate the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gone out, they would have returned finding neither family nor wealth."
"2606","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muslim, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would kiss the Yemeni Corner and place his cheek upon it."
"2607","Shayban narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, regarding the statement of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: Mankind were one nation — he said: All upon Islam. And al-Kalbi said: Meaning all upon disbelief."
"2608","Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Jumay', from one who narrated to him, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Straighten the rows, for I see the devils slipping through you as if they are the offspring of small sheep."
"2609","Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father informed me, from Qatadah, from Abu Qilabah, from Khalid ibn al-Lajlaj, from Abdullah ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw my Lord in the best form. He said to me: O Muhammad. I said: At Your service, blessed. He said: Over what does the highest assembly dispute? I said: Lord, I do not know. So He placed His hand upon my shoulders and I felt its coolness between my breasts, and I knew what is between the east and the west. Then He said: O Muhammad, over what does the highest assembly dispute? I said: Over expiations: walking on feet to Fridays, perfecting wudu in disliked circumstances, and awaiting prayer after prayer to prayer. Whoever preserves them lives well, dies well, and will be from his sins as on the day his mother bore him."
"2610","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Mubashshir narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from al-Zuhri — I think Ali ibn Husayn informed me — that Ibn Abbas said: A man from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the Ansar informed me that while they were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a star was shot and lit up. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: What would you say in the pre-Islamic period when the like of this was shot? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best; we would say: Tonight a great man was born, and tonight a great man died. He said: It is not shot for the death of anyone nor his life, but when our Lord, Blessed is Allah the Exalted, decrees a matter, the bearers of the Throne glorify, then the people of heaven next to them glorify, until the glorification reaches the people of the lowest heaven. Then they say to those next to the bearers of the Throne: What did your Lord say? So they inform them, and the people of the heavens ask one another until the news reaches the people of the lowest heaven. Then the jinn snatch the hearing and cast it to their allies, and they are shot at. What they bring as it is, is true, but they mix falsehood in it and add. The doubt is from Mubashshir."
"2611","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Yazid al-Dalani, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sleep until he snored or breathed heavily, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, you have slept. He said: Wudu is only obligatory upon one who sleeps lying down, for when he sleeps lying down his joints relax."
"2612","Amr ibn Husayn narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Ala narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked in the mirror he said: Praise be to Allah who made my form and my character good, and adorned from me what He disfigured in others. And when he applied kohl he put two in each eye and one between them, and when he wore his sandals he began with the right, and when he removed them he removed the left, and when he entered the mosque he entered his right foot, and he loved beginning with the right in everything, in taking and giving."
"2613","Amr ibn Husayn narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Ala narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Ibn Abbas who said: Sunday is a day of planting and building, Monday is a day of travel, Tuesday is a day of blood, Wednesday is a day of taking and there is no giving in it, Thursday is a day of entering upon the ruler, and Friday is a day of marriage and intercourse."
"2614","Amr ibn Husayn narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath al-Nakhai narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to me, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, a camel sacrifice became obligatory upon me but camels have become scarce, what do you think? He said: Slaughter seven sheep in its place."
"2615","Hudbah narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar who said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died when he was sixty-five years old, and al-Hasan used to say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died when he was sixty."
"2616","Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Hudayj ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Said ibn Jubayr who said: A man came to Ibn Abbas and said: The accursed Hassan has come. Ibn Abbas said: He is not accursed; he struggled alongside the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with his tongue and his self."
"2617","Suwayd ibn Said narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muhammad al-Muwaqqari narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah ibn Masud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to Caesar calling him to Islam, and sent his letter with Dihyah al-Kalbi, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to hand it to the chief of Busra so he would hand it to Caesar, so the chief of Busra handed it to Caesar. When Allah relieved Caesar of the armies of Persia, he had vowed to walk from Hims to Iliya because of what Allah had bestowed upon him in that. When the letter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached Caesar, he said when he read it: Look whether there is anyone here from his people so we may ask them about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2618","Ibn Abbas said: Abu Sufyan ibn Harb informed me that they were in Syria as merchants during the truce between the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the disbelievers of Quraysh. Abu Sufyan said: The messenger of Caesar came to us and took me and my companions until we arrived at Iliya and were admitted to him, and he was seated in his royal court wearing the crown with the nobles of Rome around. He said to his interpreter: Ask them which of them is closest to this man who claims he is a prophet. Abu Sufyan said: I am the closest of them. He said: What is your kinship? I said: He is my cousin, and there was no man of Banu Abd Manaf in the caravan that day but me. Caesar said: Bring him near me, and he ordered my companions to be placed behind my back. Then he said to his interpreter: I will ask this man about this man who claims he is a prophet, and if he lies then refute him. Abu Sufyan said: Had it not been for shame that day lest my companions report lying from me, I would have lied about him when he asked, but I was ashamed lest they report lying from me, so I told the truth about him. Then he said to his interpreter: Say: How is this man's lineage among you? I said: He is of noble lineage among us. He said: Did anyone among you ever say this before him? I said: No. He said: Did you accuse him of lying before he said what he said? I said: No. He said: Was any of his forefathers a king? I said: No. He said: Do the nobles follow him or the weak? He said: Rather the weak. He said: Do they increase or decrease? I said: Rather they increase. He said: Does he betray? I said: No, and we are now in a truce with him and we fear that. Abu Sufyan said: No word was available to me by which I could disparage him except that, for I feared it would be reported from me otherwise. He said: Did you fight him? I said: Yes. He said: How was your war and his? I said: It was alternating; he gains over us one time and we gain over him another. He said: What does he command you? I said: He commands us to worship Allah and associate nothing with Him, forbids what our fathers worshipped, and commands prayer, charity, fulfilling covenants and returning trusts. He then said to his interpreter when I said that: I asked you about his lineage and you claimed he is of noble lineage among you, and thus are messengers sent among the lineages of their people. I asked whether anyone among you said this before him and you claimed no, and I said: had one said it before him I would say a man following a saying said before him. I asked whether you accused him of lying before, and you claimed no, and I said: he would not abandon lying against people and then lie against Allah. I asked whether any forefather was a king and you claimed no, and I said: had one been a king I would say a man seeking his father's kingdom. I asked whether nobles or the weak follow him and you claimed the weak followed him, and they are the followers of the messengers. And I asked you... then he mentioned the hadith, and the hadith is in Suwayd's narration."
"2619","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Asbagh ibn Zayd al-Juhani narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, Said ibn Jubayr narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, concerning the word of Allah the Exalted: And We tried you with trials: I asked him what al-futun is. He said: Begin a new day, O Ibn Jubayr, for it has a long story. In the morning I went to Ibn Abbas to obtain what he had promised of the story of al-futun, and he said: Pharaoh and his courtiers discussed what Allah had promised Ibrahim, that He would place among his offspring prophets and kings. Some said: The Children of Israel await that without doubting, and they used to think it was Yusuf ibn Yaqub, but when he died they said: It is not so; Allah promised Ibrahim. Pharaoh said: What do you think? They deliberated and agreed to send men with knives roaming among the Children of Israel, killing every newborn male. They did so. When they saw the elders of the Children of Israel dying by their terms and the young being slaughtered, they said: You will soon annihilate the Children of Israel and come to do yourselves the labors they sufficed you, so kill every male newborn one year to reduce their growth, and leave them one year so the young grow in place of the dying elders; they will neither multiply through those you spare to outnumber you, nor perish through those you kill so you need them. They agreed on that. The mother of Musa conceived Harun in the year boys were not slaughtered and bore him openly in safety, then the next year she conceived Musa, and fear and grief fell into her heart. Allah inspired her: Do not fear nor grieve; We shall return him to you and make him among the messengers. She bore him secretly. When he was born she placed him in a chest and cast it into the sea. The sea carried it to the shore by Pharaoh's palace, and the maids found it and brought it to Pharaoh's wife Asiya. She opened it and saw a boy, and love for him was cast into her heart. She said to Pharaoh: A comfort of the eye for me and you; do not kill him. Pharaoh said: For you, but not for me. She said: I ask you by Allah except that you leave him. He left him. He was nursed by his own mother after his sister guided them to her without them perceiving, and he grew among them. One day while Pharaoh held him he pulled Pharaoh's beard; Pharaoh said: This is an enemy to me, so bring the slaughterers. Asiya said: Do not kill him, he is a child without understanding. Pharaoh said: I see understanding in him. She said: Place before him dates and live coals; if he takes the coals he is a child. They did, and he reached for the dates but the angel turned his hand to the coals, which he put in his mouth and burned his tongue, causing his lisp. So he was spared. He grew until he killed an Egyptian defending an Israelite, then fled in fear to Madyan. He arrived exhausted and sat under a tree, where he watered for two women, daughters of an old righteous man. The man invited him, married him to one of his daughters on condition of eight or ten years of hire, and gave him a staff of the prophets. He stayed, then departed with his family toward Egypt. He lost the way on a cold night and saw a fire at al-Tuwa. He went to it seeking a brand or guidance, and Allah called to him: I am Allah, Lord of the worlds; cast down your staff. It became a serpent. He was appointed a messenger and commanded to go to Pharaoh with his brother Harun. They called Pharaoh to worship Allah alone. Pharaoh demanded a sign, so Musa cast his staff and it became a manifest serpent, and drew out his hand white to the beholders. Pharaoh said to his chiefs: This is a learned sorcerer; he wants to expel you from your land. They agreed to gather the sorcerers for the appointed day of festival. Musa met them and warned them of forging lies against Allah. They cast their ropes and staffs appearing as snakes, then Musa cast his staff and it swallowed what they fabricated, and the sorcerers fell prostrate believing in the Lord of Harun and Musa. Pharaoh threatened to cut their hands and feet and crucify them, but they did not care. Allah then sent signs: the flood, locusts, lice, frogs and blood, yet they persisted. Musa departed with the Children of Israel by night; Pharaoh followed with his hosts. Allah parted the sea for Musa, they crossed, and Pharaoh and his people were drowned. Then the Children of Israel asked for a god like the idols they saw, and later worshipped the calf made by al-Samiri from the ornaments they borrowed, and Allah forgave them after repentance. Then they were commanded to enter the holy land but refused because of the tyrants therein, so they wandered forty years. This is the trial with which Allah tried Musa time after time."
"2620","Abu Yala informed us, he said: It was read to Bishr ibn al-Walid: Abu Yusuf informed you, from Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah who said: My close friend forbade me three things and commanded me three: he forbade me to peck like the pecking of the rooster, to turn like the turning of the fox, or to squat like the squatting of the beast, and he commanded me to pray witr before sleeping, to fast three days of every month, and to pray Duha."
"2621","Abu Yala informed us, he said: It was read to Bishr: Abu Yusuf informed you, from Ibn Abi Layla and al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to preach on Friday standing, then sit, then stand and preach. Ibn Abi Layla added a word, saying: So he sat a light sitting."
"2622","Abu Yala informed us, he said: It was read to Bishr: Abu Yusuf informed you, from al-Hajjaj, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), something similar to that."
"2623","Abu Yala informed us, he said: It was read to Bishr: Abu Yusuf informed you, Ismail ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Hasan and Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that Sulayk al-Ghatafani came while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was preaching on Friday, and he said: Have you prayed? He said: No. He said: Then pray two rakahs, and be brief in them."
"2624","Abu Yala informed us, he said: It was read to Bishr: Abu Yusuf informed you, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The night prayer is two by two, and when you fear dawn then pray one witr; Allah is Witr and loves witr because He is One."
"2625","Abu Yala informed us, he said: It was read to Bishr: Abu Yusuf informed you, from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn Umar, something similar to that."
"2626","Abu Yala informed us, he said: It was read to Bishr: Abu Yusuf informed you, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever catches a rakah of Friday prayer prays another one with it."
"2627","Abu Yala informed us, he said: It was read to Bishr: Abu Yusuf informed you, from al-Hajjaj, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, the same as that."
"2628","Abu Yala informed us, he said: It was read to Bishr: Abu Yusuf informed you, from Abdullah ibn al-Muharrar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Jabir, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he forbade that a dead person be followed by a voice or fire."
"2629","Abu Yala informed us, he said: It was read to Bishr: Abu Yusuf informed you, from Yahya ibn Abi Unaysah, from Zubayd al-Ayami, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: The polytheists distracted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the prayers: Zuhr, Asr, Maghrib and Isha until part of the night passed, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Bilal, who called the adhan and iqamah, then he prayed Zuhr, then ordered him and he called adhan and iqamah and he prayed Asr, then ordered him and he called adhan and iqamah and he prayed Maghrib, then ordered him and he called adhan and iqamah and he prayed Isha."
"2630","Abu Yala informed us, he said: It was read to Bishr ibn al-Walid: Abu Yusuf informed you, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Abdullah ibn Thalabah al-Udhri, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said to the martyrs of Uhud: I am a witness over these on the Day of Resurrection; shroud them with their wounds and blood, and do not wash them."
"2631","Abu Yala informed us, he said: It was read to Bishr ibn al-Walid: Abu Yusuf informed you, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas who said: Najdah wrote to him asking: Does the slave have a share of the spoils? Did women attend war with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? When does the share become due for a boy? And about the share of the near relatives? Ibn Abbas wrote to him that the slave has no right in the spoils but is given a small gift, and wrote that women used to go out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) tending the wounded and are given a gift, and that the boy has no right in the spoils until he reaches puberty, and wrote about the share of the near relatives that Umar offered us to marry our unmarried from it and pay our debts from it, but we refused him that unless he hand it over entirely, and he refused that."
"2632","Abu Yala informed us, he said: It was read to Bishr: Abu Yusuf informed you, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abu Jafar, al-Zuhri and Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Yazid ibn Hurmuz, who said: I wrote Ibn Abbas's letter to Najdah: You wrote asking about killing children, and that the learned man of Musa killed a child? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade killing children; had you known about children what the learned man of Musa knew, that would be so. And you wrote: Did women attend war with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), given a gift but no share of fay? They did attend war with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), given a gift but no share assigned. Ismail added in the hadith: And you wrote asking about slaves, did they attend war with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and was a share assigned for them? So he wrote about slaves as he wrote about women. And you wrote asking about the orphan, when he leaves orphanhood; when he reaches puberty he leaves orphanhood and a share is assigned for them."
"2633","Abu Yala informed us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami said, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Qatadah, from Anas, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever stands Laylat al-Qadr in faith and seeking reward, his past sins are forgiven."
"2634","Abu Yala narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Malik narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi narrated to us, Bahr ibn Marrar narrated to us, from his grandfather Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in his sandals."
"2635","Abu Yala informed us, Jubarah ibn Mughallis narrated to us, Sharik and Abu Shihab narrated to us, from Asim, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a bucket of Zamzam while circumambulating, and he drank standing."
"2636","Abu Yala informed us, Jubarah narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, the same as that."
"2637","Abu Yala informed us, he said: It was read to Bishr ibn al-Walid: Abu Yusuf informed you, from Amr ibn Yahya al-Ansari, from Said, freedman of Shuqran the freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that Ibn Umar narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray on a donkey while facing Khaybar."
"2638","Abu Yala informed us, he said: It was read to Bishr ibn al-Walid: Abu Yusuf informed you, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aishah, that a woman asked her about a menstruating woman making up fasts but not prayers, and she said to her: Are you a Haruri? We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and would make up fasts but not make up prayers."
"2639","Abu Yala informed us, he said: It was read to Bishr ibn al-Walid: Abu Yusuf informed you, from Abdullah ibn Ali, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah, from Talhah ibn Kaysan, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: Prayer was first obligated as two rakahs, then the resident prayer was increased and the travel prayer left as is."
"2640","Abu Yala informed us, he said: It was read to Bishr: Abu Yusuf informed you, from al-Ajlah, from Abdullah ibn Dhakwan, from al-Araj, who said: Abdullah ibn Malik ibn Buhaynah informed me that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray at night and not sit in the first two prostrations, so he prostrated two prostrations of forgetfulness in their place."
"2641","Abu Yala informed us, Muhammad ibn Jami al-Attar narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Horses have goodness tied to their forelocks."
"2642","Muhammad ibn Jami narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Goodness is tied to the forelocks of horses."
"2643","Muhammad ibn Jami al-Attar narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Goodness is tied to the forelocks of horses."
"2644","Abu Yala informed us, Muhammad ibn Uqbah al-Sadusi narrated to us, Ali Abu Muhammad al-Qurashi narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Ghanawi narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr who said: I saw the head of al-Husayn ibn Ali brought to Ubaydullah ibn Ziyad, and I saw the head of Ubaydullah ibn Ziyad brought to al-Mukhtar ibn Abi Ubayd, and I saw the head of al-Mukhtar brought to Musab ibn al-Zubayr, and I saw the head of Musab brought to Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan. Abu Yala said: These had no deed except heads."
"2645","Abu Yala informed us, Muhammad ibn Uqbah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, who said: I prepared food and invited Sulayman al-Amash, and it reached me that he said: Waddah invited us to a lean bone and sour pomegranate. I met Raqabah ibn Masqalah and complained to him, and he said: I will suffice you. He met him and said: O Abu Muhammad, a brother of ours invited you and honored you, then you say of a lean bone and sour pomegranate?! By Allah, I know you only as ill-tempered, constantly frowning, quickly bored, belittling the rights of guests, as if you are fed mustard when asked to narrate."
"2646","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, who said: I met Salamah ibn Alqamah and he narrated it to me, then retracted it, then said: When you want your companion to be disbelieved, prompt him."
"2647","Shuayb ibn Salamah ibn Qasim al-Ansari of the descendants of Rifah ibn Rafi ibn Khadij narrated to us, he said: Abu Musab Ismail ibn Qays ibn Zayd ibn Thabit narrated to us, Abu Hazim narrated to us, from Sahl ibn Sad al-Saidi who said: al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib sought permission from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to emigrate, and he said to him: O uncle, stay in your place where you are, for Allah will seal emigration with you as He sealed prophethood with me."
"2648","Yaqub narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, who said: I heard Shubah saying: This hadith preoccupation diverts you from the remembrance of Allah, from prayer and from kinship ties, so will you desist."
"2649","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Bishr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Uthman informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Mulaykah, Dhakwan narrated to me, that Ibn Abbas came seeking permission to visit Aishah while she was dying. He said: I came with Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr at her head, and I said: This is Ibn Abbas seeking permission to visit you? She said: Leave me from Ibn Abbas, I have no need of him nor his praise. Abdullah said: O mother, Abdullah ibn Abbas is among your righteous sons wanting to greet you. She said: Permit him if you wish. Ibn Abbas came and sat and said: Rejoice, for by Allah there is nothing between you and leaving every hardship and meeting Muhammad and the loved ones except your soul leaving your body. She said: Again, O Ibn Abbas? He said: You were the most beloved of the Messenger of Allah's wives to him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loved only what is pure. Your necklace fell on the day of al-Abwa, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed in the camp picking it up while people had no water, so Allah revealed that you perform tayammum with pure earth, and that was through you among what Allah revealed of concession for this ummah. Then Allah revealed your innocence from above seven heavens, so no mosque of Allah in which Allah is mentioned but your innocence is recited in it night and day. She said: Leave me from you, O Ibn Abbas, for by Allah I wish I were something forgotten and effaced."
"2650","Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Hisham ibn Yusuf narrated to us, al-Qasim nephew of Khallad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from Khallad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, that he heard Ibn Abbas saying: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was preaching on Friday, a man of Banu Layth ibn Bakr ibn Abd Manah ibn Kinanah came stepping over people until he drew near him and said: O Messenger of Allah, carry out the hadd upon me. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Sit. He sat, then stood a second time and he said: Sit. Then he stood a third time and said the same. He said: What is your hadd? He said: I came to a forbidden woman. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to some companions including Ali ibn Abi Talib, al-Abbas, Zayd ibn Harithah and Uthman ibn Affan: Take him and flog him one hundred lashes; the Laythi was unmarried. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not flog the woman with whom he sinned? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring him to me flogged. When he was brought, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who is your companion? He said: Such-and-such, a woman of Banu Bakr. He summoned her and asked her, and she said: By Allah he lied; I do not know him, and I am innocent of what he said; Allah is witness over what I say. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who witnessed that you sinned with her? She denies; if you have witnesses I will flog her, otherwise we will flog you the hadd of slander. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have no witnesses. So he ordered him flogged eighty lashes for slander."
"2651","Ishaq narrated to us, Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Ismail, from Dawud ibn Husayn, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Do not kill the dwellers of hermitages."
"2652","Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Khusayf narrated to us, Miqsam freedman of Ibn Abbas narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas who said: When this verse was revealed: It is not for a prophet to embezzle, concerning a red velvet cloth lost on the day of Badr, some people said: Perhaps the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it. So Allah revealed: It is not for a prophet to embezzle, and whoever embezzles shall bring what he embezzled on the Day of Resurrection."
"2653","Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Sawwar, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: A sheep passed in front of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying between him and the qiblah, and it did not interrupt his prayer."
"2654","Abdullah narrated to us, Abdah narrated to us, from Abu Hayyan al-Taymi, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit who said: Hassan ibn Thabit recited verses to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: And I."
"2655","Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Talhah ibn Sinan narrated to us, from Abu Sad, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to a man of the Ansar, but he delayed. He said: What detained you? He said: When your messenger came to me I was with my wife, so I got up and bathed. He said: You need not have bathed unless you ejaculated. The Ansar used to do that."
"2656","Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shrouded in a red cloak he used to wear, and a shirt."
"2657","Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn Abbas who said: When there covered the lote-tree that which covered: The Messenger of Allah said: I saw it until I fixed it firmly, then a spread of gold came between me and it."
"2658","Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Jumay, from one who narrated to him, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Straighten the rows, for I see the devils passing through you as if they are the young of al-hadhaf."
"2659","Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Abdah narrated to us, from al-Nadr ibn Arabi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas concerning the word of Allah: Look at your food and drink, it has not changed: He said: It did not alter."
"2660","Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abdullah ibn Murrah, from Masruq, from Abdullah concerning the word of Allah: We increased them in torment over torment: He said: Scorpions were added, their fangs like tall palm trees."
"2661","Surayj narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Hasan, from Ibn Abbas who said concerning His word: We increased them in torment over torment: He said: They are five rivers beneath the Throne; they are tormented with some by night and some by day."
"2662","Muhriz ibn Awn narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf narrated to us, from his father, from Talhah ibn Abdullah ibn Awf who said: I prayed behind Ibn Abbas over a funeral, and he recited the Fatihah and a surah aloud until we heard him. When he finished I took his hand and asked him about that, and he said: It is sunnah and right."
"2663","Mahmud ibn Khidash narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Talhah, from Ibn Abbas who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left Makkah he said: By Allah, I shall leave you, and I know you are the most beloved of Allah's lands to me and most honored to Allah; had your people not expelled me I would not have left. O Banu Abd Manaf, if you become rulers of this affair after me, do not prevent any circumambulator at Allah's House for an hour of night or day. Had Quraysh not transgressed I would have told them what is for them with Allah. O Allah, You made the first of them taste affliction, so make the last of them taste favor."
"2664","Muhammad al-Ahmasi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, al-Kalbi narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Ibn Abbas, concerning His word: And We sent down from the rain-laden clouds pouring water: He said: Al-muirat are the winds; thajjaja means pouring forth."
"2665","And from Ibn Abbas concerning His word: Or like a rainstorm from the sky: He said: Al-sayyib is rain."
"2666","And from Ibn Abbas concerning His word: Gentle wherever it befalls: He said: Al-rukha is the obedient; as for His word: Wherever it befalls, he said: Wherever it wills. And concerning His word: He sends the winds stirring clouds and spreads them in the sky as He wills and makes them fragments: He says: Pieces, some above others; Then you see the rain meaning the rain coming forth from between them, from among them."
"2667","And from Ibn Abbas, concerning His word: A whirlwind with fire therein and it burned: He said: Al-isar is the violent wind."
"2668","And from Ibn Abbas, concerning His word: Confused dreams: He said: They are lying dreams."
"2669","And from Ibn Abbas, concerning the word of Allah: Those who consume usury do not stand except as one whom Satan prostrates by touch stands: He said: They are known on the Day of Resurrection by that; they cannot stand except as the insane strangled one stands. That is because they said: Trade is like usury, and they lied against Allah. Allah permitted trade and forbade usury; whoever receives admonition from his Lord and desists, up to His word: And whoever returns and eats usury, those are companions of the Fire abiding therein. And His word: O you who believe, fear Allah and leave what remains of usury if you are believers; if you do not, then take notice of war from Allah, to the end of the verse. It reached us, and Allah knows best, that this verse was revealed concerning Banu Amr ibn Umayr ibn Awf of Thaqif and Banu al-Mughirah of Banu Makhzum; Banu al-Mughirah used to take usury from Thaqif. When Allah gave His Messenger victory over Makkah, he abolished all usury that day. The people of Taif had made peace on condition of their usury, and what was owed upon them of usury was abolished. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote at the end of their document: They have what Muslims have and upon them what is upon Muslims, that they shall not eat usury nor feed it. Banu Amr ibn Umayr and Banu al-Mughirah came to Attab ibn Asid, who was over Makkah. Banu al-Mughirah said: What made us the most wretched of people through usury? It was abolished from people but us. Banu Amr ibn Umayr said: We were conciliated on condition of our usury. Attab ibn Asid wrote about that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and this verse was revealed: If you do not, then take notice of war from Allah and His Messenger. Banu Amr knew that they had no power for war from Allah and His Messenger, so they left it."
"2670","Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, Waki ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, from a shaykh Waki named, who said: I heard Tawus narrating from Abdullah al-Azdi or Ubaydullah al-Azdi, Abu Uthman doubted, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was inspired to prostrate upon seven bones, and not to gather hair nor garment."
"2671","Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Aslam informed me, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rinsed his mouth, sniffed water, washed his face, washed his forearms once and his hand once, and wiped his head and ears. And one of our companions informed me that Ibn Abbas said: And he washed his feet."
"2672","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, he said: Ata narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed wudu rinsing and sniffing from a single handful."
"2673","Nasr ibn Ali ibn Nasr al-Jahdami narrated to us, Musa ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, Abu Musa al-Saffar narrated to us, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas, or he was asked: Which charity is best? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best charity is water. Have you not heard the people of the Fire when they seek help from the people of Paradise saying: Pour upon us some water or of what Allah has provided you."
"2674","al-Hasan ibn Shabib narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Allah I shall raid Quraysh, by Allah I shall raid Quraysh, by Allah I shall raid Quraysh, if Allah wills, from my memory of this, or the like."
"2675","Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Misar ibn Kidam, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Allah I shall raid Quraysh, by Allah I shall raid Quraysh, by Allah I shall raid Quraysh, then he fell silent a while and said: If Allah wills."
"2676","Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Habib, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: How are you this morning? He said: Well, better than people who did not visit a sick person nor attend a funeral."
"2677","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Makhramah ibn Bukayr narrated to me, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: The night prayer was mentioned, and some said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Half of it, a third of it, a quarter of it, the time of milking a camel, the time of milking a sheep."
"2678","Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Qays, Salih freedman of al-Tawamah narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Zuhr and Asr, and Maghrib and Isha, without travel or rain. He said: I said: What did he intend by that? He said: He intended latitude for his ummah."
"2679","Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Ashath, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: Damrah ibn Jundub left his house emigrating and said to his family: Carry me and take me out of the land of the polytheists to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He died on the way before reaching the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and revelation descended: And whoever leaves his house emigrating to Allah and His Messenger then death overtakes him, until it reached: And Allah is Forgiving, Merciful."
"2680","Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Abdah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Masud ibn Malik, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was aided by al-saba wind, and Ad were destroyed by al-dabur."
"2681","Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, Aththam ibn Ali narrated to us, al-Amash informed us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray two rakahs of the night, then leave and use the siwak."
"2682","Sulayman Abu Ayyub al-Shadhakuni narrated to me, he said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from Sufyan, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Qatadah concerning spoils he had taken: Leave it and its spoils."
"2683","Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Bakr ibn Wail, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas who said: Sad ibn Ubadah came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My mother died with an unfulfilled vow. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Fulfill it on her behalf."
"2684","Muadh ibn Shubah narrated to us, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, Hilal ibn Khabbab narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at Uhud and said: It would not please me that it were gold for the family of Muhammad which I spend in Allah's cause, dying the day I die with two dinars of it with me."
"2685","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Ubaydullah al-Ashjai narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Hakim ibn al-Daylami, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn Abbas: And you are samidun: He said: They used to pass by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) haughtily. Have you not seen how the calf struts haughtily."
"2686","Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proposed to a Qurashi woman called Sawdah, and said to her: The best women who rode camels are the women of Quraysh, most affectionate to a child in his infancy, and most careful of a husband in his property."
"2687","Muhriz narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in a garment wrapped around him, its ends crossed, shielding himself with its excess from the heat and cold of the ground."
"2688","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, he said: I heard Layth, from Abu Fazarah, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was not commanded to decorate mosques."
"2689","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, he said: I heard my father saying: Abu Hamzah informed us, from Layth, from Abu Fazarah, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was not commanded to decorate mosques."
"2690","Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Said, from Ali ibn al-Hakam, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade on the day of Khaybar every fanged beast of prey and every taloned bird."
"2691","Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Said, he said: I heard al-Nadr ibn Anas saying: I was with Ibn Abbas when they began asking him for fatwas, and he gave them fatwas without mentioning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in them, until a man of Iraq came, I think, and said: I make these pictures. He said: Come near, come near, two or three times. I heard Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever makes a picture in this world will be charged on the Day of Resurrection to breathe a soul into it, and he will not breathe."
"2692","Musa ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Hajjaj informed us, from Husayn ibn Abdullah ibn Ubaydullah ibn Abbas, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There is no harm for a man to enter ihram in a garment dyed with saffron that has been washed, having neither lint nor redness."
"2693","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Five the muhrim kills: the kite, the mouse, the scorpion, the crow and the vicious dog."
"2694","Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Abbad ibn Mansur narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a kohl container with which he applied kohl at sleep, three times in each eye."
"2695","Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died while his armor was pawned with a Jewish man for twenty sa of barley he took as food for his family."
"2696","Musa narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Salamah, from al-Hasan al-Urani, from Ibn Abbas who said: When you have stoned the jamrah, everything becomes lawful for you except women. A man said: O Abu al-Abbas: perfume? He said: As for me, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) scenting his head with musk; is that perfume or not?"
"2697","Musa narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) continued talbiyah until he stoned the jamrah."
"2698","Musa narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Habib, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: No believing man hates the Ansar, or: except that Allah and His Messenger hate him."
"2699","Musa narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bashir, from Abdullah ibn al-Musawir who said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not a believer who eats his fill while his neighbor is hungry beside him."
"2700","Musa narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Aishah and Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the tawaf of the Day of Sacrifice until night."
"2701","Musa narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abis who said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: I went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a feast day; he prayed, then preached, then came to the women, admonished and reminded them and ordered them to give charity."
"2702","Musa narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Tamimi, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used the siwak so much that we saw, or feared, it would be revealed upon him."
"2703","Musa narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray upon a mat."
"2704","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Kathir narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Tawus prayed beside me; when he prostrated the first prostration and raised his head he raised his hands facing his face, and I disapproved. I said to Wuhayb ibn Khalid: He does something I never saw anyone do. Wuhayb said to him: You do something we never saw anyone do? Abdullah ibn Tawus said: I saw my father do it; my father said: I saw Ibn Abbas do it. He mentioned that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do it."
"2705","Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Yahya narrated to me, from al-Hakam ibn Aban, from Ikrimah who said: Ibn Abbas said: Allah did not secure any of His creation except Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: That Allah may forgive you your past and future sins, the verse; and He said to the angels: Whoever of them says: I am a god besides Him, him We shall recompense with Hell."
"2706","Abu Mamar narrated to us, Abd al-Salam narrated to us, from Yazid al-Dalani, from al-Hasan who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to touch his beard in prayer."
"2707","Bundar narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman al-Bakrawi narrated to us, from Ismail al-Makki, from Abu Raja, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Guard against the Fire even with half a date."
"2708","Abu Mamar narrated to us, Ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Arqam ibn Shurahbil, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took up recitation where Abu Bakr had left off."
"2709","Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I heard Khusayf, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas who said: No rafath: Rafath is intercourse; Nor fusuq: Fusuq is sins; Nor jidal in Hajj: Jidal is disputation."
"2710","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas and others, from al-Hasan, both said: When the verse of debt was revealed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first to deny was Adam; the first to deny was Adam. When Allah created him He wiped his back and brought forth what would issue from him, and displayed them to him. He saw among them a shining man and said: O Lord, which of my sons is this? He said: Your son Dawud. He said: O Lord, how long is his life? He said: Sixty years. He said: O Lord, add to his life. He said: No, unless you add from your own life. Adam's life was a thousand years, so he granted him forty years of his life. Allah wrote a document and had the angels witness it. When Adam was dying, angels came to take him, and he said: Forty years of my life remain. They said: You granted them to your son Dawud. He said: I did not do it. Allah produced the document and the angels bore witness, and Adam was completed a thousand years and Dawud a hundred years."
"2711","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Sulaym ibn Muslim al-Makki narrated to us, Nadr ibn Arabi narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One who drinks in gold and silver vessels only gurgles Hellfire in his belly."
"2712","Humayd ibn Masadah narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Habib narrated to us, from Awf, from Said ibn Abi al-Hasan, from Ibn Abbas who said: Whoever abandons Friday three consecutive Fridays has cast Islam behind his back."
"2713","Bishr ibn Sayhan narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The best you change gray hair with is henna and katam."
"2714","Hajjaj ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad and Hujayn ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Yunus said: Hibban ibn Ali narrated to us, from Uqayl, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best companions are four, the best detachments four hundred, the best armies four thousand, and no people of twelve thousand are defeated through fewness if they are truthful and patient; except Hujayn said: from Ibn Shihab, and did not say at the end: and patient."
"2715","Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to trim his mustache, and Ibrahim used to trim his mustache."
"2716","Abu Yala informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The little finger and the thumb are equal."
"2717","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Husayn al-Muallim informed us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from Tawus, who heard Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: It is not lawful for a Muslim man to give a gift then take it back, except a father in what he gives his child; the one who takes back his gift is like a dog that ate until full then vomited, then returned to its vomit."
"2718","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of al-Hudaybiyah: May Allah have mercy on those who shave. They said: And those who shorten, O Messenger of Allah? He said: May Allah have mercy on those who shave. They said: And those who shorten, O Messenger of Allah? He said: May Allah have mercy on those who shave. They said: And those who shorten, O Messenger of Allah? He said: And those who shorten. They said: O Messenger of Allah, why did you favor those who shave with mercy? He said: They did not doubt."
"2719","Zuhayr narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Thabit Abu Zayd narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym uncle of Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This Stone has a tongue and two lips bearing witness for whoever touches it in truth on the Day of Resurrection."
"2720","Zuhayr narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Thabit Abu Zayd narrated to us, from Hilal, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken by night to Bayt al-Maqdis, then came in the night and told them of his journey, the sign of Bayt al-Maqdis and their caravan. He said: Some people said: We do not believe Muhammad, and apostatized as disbelievers; Allah struck their necks with Abu Jahl. Abu Jahl said: Does Muhammad frighten us with the tree of Zaqqum? Bring dates and butter; let us eat greedily. He said: And he saw the Dajjal in his form with the eye, not a dream, and Isa son of Maryam, and Ibrahim. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the Dajjal? He said: I saw him bulky, fair, light-skinned; one eye standing as if a glittering star, his hair as if branches of a tree. I saw Isa: a young white man, curly-haired, sharp-sighted, compactly built. I saw Musa: dark, dusky, thick-haired, strongly built. I saw Ibrahim, and I look at no limb of his but I look at him as if your companion. Jibril said to me: Greet your father, and I greeted him."
"2721","In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. The venerable shaykh Abu Sad ibn Abi Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Janzarudhi informed us, reading to him and he acknowledged it saying: Yes. Abu Amr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Muqri al-Hiri informed us in the year 370, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili al-Tamimi informed us in the year 306, Zuhayr narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Awanah Waddah narrated to us, from Abd al-Ala, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of narrating from me except what you know, for whoever lies upon me deliberately shall take his seat in the Fire, and whoever lies about the Quran without knowledge shall take his seat in the Fire."
"2722","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi al-Furat narrated to us, from Ilba, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drew four lines on the ground and said: Do you know what this is? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best women of Paradise are Khadijah bint Khuwaylid, Fatimah bint Muhammad, Maryam bint Imran, and Asiyah bint Muzahim wife of Pharaoh."
"2723","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Talhah ibn Nafi mentioned, from Said, from Abdullah ibn Abbas who said: An Ansari man married a woman of Banu Ajlan; he consummated with her and stayed the night, and in the morning said: I did not find her a virgin. Their case was raised to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he summoned the girl and asked her, and she said: Yes, I was a virgin. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered them to invoke mutual curses, and gave her the dowry."
"2724","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ahwas ibn Jawwab al-Dabbi narrated to us, Ammar ibn Zurayq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abd al-Karim, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade gold rings, qassiyah garments, red saddle cloths saturated with safflower, and reciting the Quran while bowing or prostrating."
"2725","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ahwas ibn Jawwab al-Dabbi narrated to us, Ammar ibn Zurayq narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Amash, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Zuhr on the day of Tarwiyah and Fajr on the day of Arafah are at Mina."
"2726","Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Asadi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married while in ihram, and cupped while in ihram."
"2727","Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Asadi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of your kohls at sleep is ithmid; it grows hair and clears sight. The best of your garments are white; wear them and shroud your dead in them."
"2728","Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Asadi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Arqam ibn Abi al-Arqam al-Zuhri over some charity; he passed by Abu Rafi and took him along. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. He said: O Abu Rafi, charity is unlawful for Muhammad and the family of Muhammad; the freedman of a people is from them, or from themselves."
"2729","Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Asadi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ali ibn Badhimah, from Qays ibn Habtar who said: I asked Ibn Abbas about white, green and red jars. He said: The first to ask the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the delegation of Abd al-Qays. He said: Do not drink in gourds, varnished vessels, hollowed stumps or hantam, nor drink in jars; drink in skins. He said: So pour water upon it. On the third or fourth he said to him: Pour it out. Then he said: Allah has forbidden me, or: He forbade, wine, gambling, the kubah; and every intoxicant is unlawful. Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I said to Ali ibn Badhimah: What is al-kubah? He said: The drum."
"2730","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak informed us, Husayn ibn Abdullah ibn Ubaydullah ibn Abbas informed us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade naqir, gourds and varnished vessels, and said: Do not drink except in a vessel. So they made camel skins with necks of sheep skins. When that reached him he said: Do not drink except in what is covered thereof."
"2731","Abu Abbad Qatan ibn Nusayr al-Ghabari narrated to us, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Abu Rafi who said: Abu Luluah was a slave of al-Mughirah ibn Shubah and used to make millstones; al-Mughirah taxed him four dirhams daily. Abu Luluah met Umar and said: O Commander of the Faithful, al-Mughirah has burdened my tax; speak to him to lighten it. Umar said to him: Fear Allah and do good to your master; Umar intended to meet al-Mughirah and ask him to lighten it. The slave grew angry and said: His justice encompassed all people but me. He resolved to kill him and fashioned a double-bladed dagger, sharpened and poisoned it, then brought it to al-Hurmuzan asking: How do you see this? He said: I think you strike no one with it but you kill him. Abu Luluah waited and came at dawn prayer, standing behind Umar; when prayer was established Umar would speak saying: Straighten your rows, as he used to say. When he said takbir, Abu Luluah stabbed him in the shoulder and in the side; Umar fell, and he stabbed thirteen men with his dagger, seven dying and six surviving. Umar was carried to his house, and people clamored until sunrise nearly came. Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf called: O people, prayer, prayer, prayer. They hastened to prayer, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf led them with the two shortest surahs of the Quran. When he finished, they turned to Umar. He called for a drink to see his wound; nabidh was brought and he drank, and it came out of his wound, none knowing whether it was nabidh or blood. Milk was called for and he drank, and it came out of his wound. They said: No harm upon you, O Commander of the Faithful. He said: If killing has harm, I have been killed. People praised him saying: May Allah reward you well, O Commander of the Faithful; you were and you were. Then they left and others came praising him. Umar said: By Allah, for what you say, I wish I could leave it even, neither for nor against me, and that my companionship of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had remained safe for me. Abdullah ibn Abbas spoke, being at his head as his close companion as of his family; Ibn Abbas recited the Quran. Abdullah ibn Abbas spoke saying: By Allah, you shall not leave it even; you accompanied the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the best companionship, you were to him and you were to him and you were to him, until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away pleased with you. Then you accompanied the successor of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then you ruled it, O Commander of the Faithful, ruling in the best manner; you did and you did. Umar found comfort in Ibn Abbas's talk and said: O Ibn Abbas, repeat your talk to me. He repeated it. Umar said: By Allah, for what you say, had I the earth full of gold I would ransom myself today from the terror of the ascent. I have made it consultation among six: Uthman, Ali, Talhah ibn Ubaydullah, al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf and Sad ibn Abi Waqqas; I placed Abdullah ibn Umar with them as adviser but not of them, gave them three days, and ordered Suhayb to lead people in prayer."
"2732","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Abu Jamrah informed us, that he used to sit with Ibn Abbas and keep people from him. He said: I was kept from him some days, and he said to me: What kept you? I said: Fever. He said to me: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fever is from the heat of Hell, so extinguish it from yourselves with Zamzam water."
"2733","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Makhlad ibn Yazid al-Harrani narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Yusuf, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, that he saw Abu Hurayrah performing wudu and he said: O Ibn Abbas, do you know from what I perform wudu? From crumbs of cheese I ate. He said: By Allah, I do not know from what you performed wudu? As for me, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eat bread and meat, then stand for prayer without performing wudu."
"2734","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Makhlad ibn Yazid narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Umar ibn Ata ibn Abi al-Khuwar, from Ibn Abbas who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eat a bone with meat, then the caller to prayer came, so he put it down and stood for prayer without touching water."
"2735","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Majid al-Hanafi narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Tamam, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade branding on the face; when al-Abbas heard that, he branded on the two sides of the rump."
"2736","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Yaqub al-Qummi narrated to us, Jafar narrated to us, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I am ruined. He said: What ruined you? He said: I turned my saddle last night. He did not answer him. This verse was revealed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Your women are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish: meaning: approach from front or back, but avoid the anus and menstruation."
"2737","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the sister of Uqbah ibn Amir vowed to perform Hajj walking; he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah is free of your sister's vow; let her ride andsacrifice a sacrificial camel."
"2738","Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Umayyah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was forbidden to pray behind talkers and sleepers."
"2739","Zuhayr narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Yazid ibn Hurmuz, that Najdah al-Haruri when he rose in the fitnah of Ibn al-Zubayr sent to Ibn Abbas asking about the share of the near relatives, for whom he sees it? He said: It is for the near relatives of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided it for them. Umar had offered us an offer we deemed less than our right, so we returned it to him and refused to accept it; what he offered them was to aid their marrier, pay their debtor and give their poor, refusing to add beyond that."
"2740","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Abbad ibn Mansur informed us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: When was revealed: Those who accuse chaste women then bring not four witnesses, flog them eighty lashes and accept not their testimony ever; those are the defiantly disobedient: Sad ibn Ubadah, chief of the Ansar, said: Was it revealed so, O Messenger of Allah? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Ansar, do you not hear what your chief says? They said: O Messenger of Allah, do not blame him; he is a jealous man; by Allah he never married but a virgin, nor divorced a woman but no man of us dared marry her from his jealousy. Sad said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I know it is true and from Allah, but I wonder that if I found a wicked woman with a man upon her, I may not disturb nor move him until I bring four witnesses? By Allah I shall not bring them until he finishes his need. Shortly after, Hilal ibn Umayyah came, one of the three whose repentance was accepted; he came from his land at night and found a man with his wife; he saw with his eyes and heard with his ears, and did not disturb him until morning. He went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O Messenger of Allah, I came to my wife at night and found a man with her; I saw with my eyes and heard with my ears. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked what he brought and it weighed upon him; the Ansar gathered saying: We are afflicted with what Sad ibn Ubadah said, unless the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) flogs Hilal ibn Umayyah and nullifies his testimony among Muslims. He said: By Allah, by Allah, I hope Allah will make for me a way out. Hilal said: O Messenger of Allah, I see what weighs upon you of what I brought, and Allah knows I am truthful. By Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was about to order him flogged when revelation descended upon him; when revelation descended they knew it by the trembling of his skin, so they held back until the revelation finished. There was revealed: Those who accuse their wives and have no witnesses but themselves, the whole verse. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was relieved and said: Rejoice, O Hilal; Allah has made for you relief and a way out. Hilal said: I hoped that from my Lord. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Send for her. They sent for her and she came. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited it to them, reminded them and told them the torment of the Hereafter is severer than of this world. Hilal said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I told truth about her. She said: He lied. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Invoke curses between them. He said to Hilal: Testify. He testified four testimonies by Allah that he is truthful. At the fifth it was said: O Hilal, fear Allah, for worldly torment is lighter than Hereafter torment, and this is the decisive one incurring torment. He said: By Allah, Allah shall not torment me for it as He did not flog me for it. He testified the fifth that Allah's curse be upon him if he is among liars. Then she was told: Testify. She testified four testimonies by Allah that he is among liars. At the fifth it was said to her: Fear Allah, for worldly torment is lighter than Hereafter torment, and this is the decisive one incurring torment upon you. She hesitated a while, then said: By Allah I shall not disgrace my people. She testified the fifth that Allah's wrath be upon her if he is truthful. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) separated them, decreed her child be attributed to no father, nor her child be accused, and whoever accuses her or her child incurs the hadd; decreed she has no lodging nor sustenance from him since they separate without divorce nor death; and said: If she bears him small, slight, flat-nosed, thin-shanked, he is Hilal's; if she bears him dark, curly, bulky, thick-shanked, full-buttocked, he is the accused one's. She bore him dark, curly, bulky, thick-shanked, full-buttocked. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not for oaths, I and she would have had a matter. Ikrimah said: He later became a governor over Egypt and is attributed to no father."
"2741","Abu Yala informed us, my father narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, similarly."
"2742","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Fitr, from Shurahbil ibn Sad, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Muslim man having two daughters, treating them well as long as they accompany him or he accompanies them, but they shall admit him to Paradise."
"2743","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whomever you find coming to an animal, kill him and kill it with him; and whomever you find doing the deed of the people of Lut, kill the doer and the one done to."
"2744","Zuhayr narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Umar narrated to me that Ata informed him that Abdullah ibn Abbas invited al-Fadl ibn Abbas to food on the day of Arafah. He said: I am fasting. Abdullah said: Do not fast, for milk in a milking vessel was brought near to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he drank from it on this day, and people follow your example."
"2745","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the eclipse prayer and heard not a letter from him in it."
"2746","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said: O you who believe, obey Allah and obey the Messenger and those in authority among you, concerning Abdullah ibn Hudhafah ibn Qays ibn Adi, whom the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent on a detachment. Yala ibn Muslim informed it to me, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas."
"2747","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, from Tawus, reaching the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Nothing like marriage was seen for two who love one another."
"2748","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, from Ubayd ibn Sad, reaching the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever loves my natural way shall follow my sunnah, and marriage is of my sunnah."
"2749","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Hakam, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Abu al-Sahba who said: I was with Ibn Abbas when we mentioned what interrupts prayer. They said: The donkey and the woman. Ibn Abbas said: I came with a boy of Banu Abd al-Muttalib riding behind me on a donkey, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying with people on open ground. We left the donkey in front of them, then came until we entered among them, and he did not mind that. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying with people when two slave girls of Banu Abd al-Muttalib came running, fighting one another; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took them and separated one from the other, and did not mind that."
"2750","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Ayyash ibn Abi Rabiah, from Hakim ibn Hakim ibn Abbad ibn Hunayf, from Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Jibril led me at the House twice. He prayed Zuhr when the sun declined, the length of a sandal strap, then prayed Asr when every shadow was its length, then prayed Maghrib with me when the fasting person breaks fast, then prayed Isha with me when the twilight vanished, then prayed Fajr when food and drink become forbidden to the fasting person. Then he prayed Zuhr the next day when everything was its shadow's length, then prayed Asr when everything was twice its shadow, then prayed Maghrib with me when the fasting person breaks fast at one time, then prayed Isha when the first third of the night had gone, then prayed Fajr, I know not what he said, then turned to me saying: O Muhammad, this is the time of the prophets before you; the time is between these two times."
"2751","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, al-Mutamir narrated to us, from his father, from Hanash, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever combines two prayers without excuse has come to a door of the major sins; and whoever conceals testimony seizing thereby a Muslim's property, or shedding thereby his blood, has incurred the Fire, or as he said."
"2752","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Abd Rabbihi ibn Bariq al-Hanafi narrated to us, that he heard his grandfather Simak al-Hanafi narrating from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Aishah, whoever of my ummah has two forerunners enters Paradise through them. She said: May my father be ransom, and whoever has one forerunner? He said: And whoever has one forerunner, O Muwaffaqah. She said: May my father be ransom, and whoever of your ummah has no forerunner? He said: I am the forerunner of my ummah; they were afflicted with none like me."
"2753","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn al-Akhnas narrated to us, Ibn Abi Mulaykah narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As if I look at him, black, bow-legged, uprooting it stone by stone, meaning the Kabah."
"2754","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Bakri narrated to us, Amr ibn Malik narrated to us, from Abu al-Jawza, from Ibn Abbas concerning the word of Allah: By your life: He said: By your life."
"2755","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Nahik, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever asks you by Allah's Face, give him; and whoever seeks refuge with you by Allah, grant him refuge."
"2756","Musnad of Anas ibn Malik. What al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan narrated from Anas ibn Malik. (2756) - Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Tamimi al-Mawsili informed us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, al-Hasan narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to deliver the Friday sermon beside a wooden post, leaning his back against it. When the people grew numerous, he said: Build a pulpit for me. So they built for him a pulpit with two steps. When he stood on the pulpit to preach, the wooden post moaned toward the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Anas said: And I was in the mosque, and I heard the wood when it moaned, moaning like one distracted with grief. It kept moaning until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came down to it and embraced it, and it fell quiet. He said: Al-Hasan, when he narrated this hadith, would weep, then say: O servants of Allah, the wood moans toward the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) out of longing for him because of his station with Allah, so you are more entitled to long to meet him."
"2757","(2757) - Abu Ibrahim al-Tarjuman narrated to us, Salih al-Murri narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Hasan narrating from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in what he reports from his Lord, he said: Four traits: one of them is for Me, one is for you, one is between Me and you, and one is between you and My servants. As for what is for Me, it is that you worship Me and associate nothing with Me. As for what is for you from Me, it is that whatever good you do, I reward you for it. As for what is between Me and you, supplication is from you and answering is upon Me. And as for what is between you and My servants, it is that you approve for them what you approve for yourself."
"2758","(2758) - Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Mubarak narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Hasan, from Anas, that a man said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When is the Hour? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed it is coming to pass, so what have you prepared for it? He said: I have not prepared much for it, except that I love Allah and His Messenger. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then you are with whom you loved, and for you is what you reckoned. Then he said: You ask me about the Hour, and by the One in whose Hand is my soul, there is not upon the earth a living soul today upon which a hundred years will pass. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, then said: Where is the one who asked about the Hour? So the man was brought, his sinews trembling. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at a boy from Daws called Sa'd and said: If this one lives, he will not grow old before the Hour comes. Anas said: And I on that day was about the size of the boy."
"2759","(2759) - Al-Hasan ibn Hammad and Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, and the wording is al-Hasan's, they said: Hazm ibn Mihran al-Quta'i narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out one day to one of his outings, and with him were some of his Companions, and they set off walking. The time of prayer came, so the people dismounted and found no water with which to perform ablution. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we find nothing with which to perform ablution. And he saw dislike in the faces of his Companions. A man from the people went off and brought a small cup containing a little water. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it and performed ablution from it, then passed his four fingers over the cup, then said to the people: Come on. He said: So the people came and performed ablution until they completed what they wanted of ablution. It was said: How many did the people reach? He said: Seventy men, or about that."
"2760","(2760) - Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Maymun ibn Najih Abu al-Hasan al-Naji narrated to us, al-Hasan narrated to us, from Anas, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I desire jihad but I am not able to do it. He said: Is anyone of your parents still left? He said: My mother. He said: Then exert yourself for Allah in dutifulness to her. If you do that, then you are a pilgrim performing Hajj, a performer of Umrah, and a warrior. So when your mother is pleased with you, then fear Allah and honor her."
"2761","(2761) - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salam Abu Harb narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan, from Anas, that the Hawd (Pool) was mentioned in the presence of Ubayd Allah ibn Ziyad, and it was as if he denied it. That reached Anas, so he said: By no means, I shall surely displease him. So he came to him and said: What is it you denied about the Hawd? He said: Did you hear it, O Abu Hamzah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes, more than such-and-such times. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: What is between the two ends of my Pool is like what is between Aylah and Makkah, or between Sanaa and Makkah. And its vessels are more numerous than the number of the stars of the sky."
"2762","(2762) - Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Isma'il, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of my Companions is like salt in food; food is not good except with salt."
"2763","(2763) - Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Isma'il, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to a man driving a sacrificial camel barefoot, and said: Ride it. He said: O Messenger of Allah, it is a sacrificial animal. He said: Ride it. So he rode it."
"2764","(2764) - Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Nuh, from Ayyub, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says: I am indeed shy to leave My servant, man or woman, who grows grey in Islam, so that the beard of My servant and the head of My maidservant turn grey in Islam, and then I punish them in the Fire after that."
"2765","(2765) - Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Yusuf ibn Abi Kathir, from Nuh ibn Dhakwan, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Part of extravagance is that you eat everything you desire."
"2766","(2766) - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Muslim, from al-Hasan and Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not trade in uncertainty (gharar)."
"2767","(2767) - Humayd ibn Mas'adah al-Sami narrated to us, Ar'arah ibn al-Birind narrated to us, Isma'il al-Makki narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not touch-bargain (mulamasah), do not engage in false bidding (najsh), do not trade in uncertainty, a town-dweller must not sell for a bedouin, and whoever buys a she-camel whose milk has been withheld (muhhaffalah), let him milk it for three days; if he returns it, let him return it with a sa' of dates."
"2768","(2768) - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Isma'il narrated to us, from al-Hasan and Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say the Talbiyah: Here I am, O Allah, here I am; here I am, there is no partner for You, here I am; indeed praise and blessing are Yours, and dominion; there is no partner for You."
"2769","(2769) - Abu Kurayb Muhammad ibn al-Ala narrated to us, Mus'ab ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, from Mubarak ibn Fadalah, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: When death descended upon the Messenger of Allah, Fatimah said: O my distress! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O my daughter, there will be no distress upon your father after today."
"2770","(2770) - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Umar ibn Musawir al-Ijli, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never intended a journey except that he said, when he rose from his sitting: O Allah, by You I spread out, to You I turn, and by You I hold fast. O Allah, You are my trust and You are my hope. O Allah, suffice me in what concerns me and what I do not concern myself with, and what You know better of me than I do. Provision me with piety, forgive my sin, and direct me to good wherever I turn. He said: Then he would go out."
"2771","(2771) - Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Muslim, from al-Hasan and Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has two tongues in this world, Allah will make for him two tongues of Fire."
"2772","(2772) - Humayd ibn Mas'adah al-Sami narrated to us, from Ar'arah ibn al-Birind, Isma'il al-Makki narrated to us, from al-Hasan and Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has two tongues in this world, Allah will make for him two tongues in the Fire of the Day of Resurrection."
"2773","(2773) - Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Yazid ibn Aban, from al-Hasan, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the Qur'an is richness after which there is no poverty, and there is no richness apart from it."
"2774","(2774) - Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Abu Sa'id, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, from Mubarak, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: Prices rose in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so they said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you would fix prices for us? So he said: Indeed Allah is the Withholder, the Extender. I withhold from you and I do not give it to you. I hope to meet Allah while none of you seeks from me redress for an injustice I did to him in life or wealth."
"2775","(2775) - Al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, Mubashshir ibn Isma'il al-Halabi narrated to us, from Tammam ibn Najih, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are no two guardian angels who raise to Allah what they guarded, and Allah sees at the beginning of the page good or at its end, except that Allah says to His angels: Bear witness that I have forgiven My servant what is between the two ends of the page."
"2776","(2776) - Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan Abu Hammam al-Ahwazi narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A town-dweller must not sell for a bedouin, even if he is his brother or his father."
"2777","(2777) - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hafs narrated to us, from Ash'ath, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A person is with whom he loved."
"2778","(2778) - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most beloved names to Allah are: Abd Allah, Abd al-Rahman, and al-Harith."
"2779","(2779) - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Abi Rabi'ah, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three to whom Paradise longs: Ali, Ammar, and Salman."
"2780","(2780) - Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Abi Rabi'ah, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise longs for three: Ali, Ammar, and Salman."
"2781","(2781) - Al-Hasan ibn Umar ibn Shaqiq al-Jarmi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Muslim, from al-Hasan, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray upon his mount."
"2782","(2782) - Abu Yusuf al-Jizi narrated to us, Mu'ammal narrated to us, Mubarak informed us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and with him was Umar ibn al-Khattab, and the Messenger of Allah was on a bed woven with cord, with nothing between the side of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the cord. He was the most delicate of people in skin. He shifted a movement and the cord had left a mark on the skin of his belly or his side, so Umar wept. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What makes you weep? He said: By Allah, I weep, O Messenger of Allah, not but that I know you are nobler to Allah than Caesar and Khosrau; they revel in what they revel in of this world, while you are the Messenger of Allah in the state I see? So he said: O Umar, are you not pleased that the Hereafter be ours and this world theirs? He said: Yes indeed. He said: Then it is so."
"2783","(2783) - Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us, al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, from al-Mubarak ibn Fadalah, from al-Hasan, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a bed woven with cord. Some of his Companions entered upon him, and Umar entered. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shifted, and the cord had left a mark on his side. Umar wept and said: By Allah, we know you are nobler to Allah than Khosrau and Caesar, while they revel in what they revel in. He said: Are you not pleased that this world be theirs and the Hereafter ours? He said: Yes indeed. He said: Then he fell silent."
"2784","(2784) - Amr ibn al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Salim al-Khayyat, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: I never smelled musk nor ambergris with a scent more pleasant than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2785","(2785) - Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Habib ibn al-Shahid, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out intending the mosque, leaning upon Usamah ibn Zayd, wearing a cotton garment wrapped around him, and he led them in prayer."
"2786","(2786) - Harun ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Mas'adah narrated to us, from Imran al-Qummi, from al-Hasan, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I kept interceding to my Lord and He kept granting my intercession, until I say: My Lord, grant me intercession for whoever said: There is no god but Allah. He says: This is not for you, O Muhammad; it is for Me. But by My might, My forbearance, and My mercy, I shall not leave in the Fire anyone - or he said: a servant - who said: There is no god but Allah."
"2787","(2787) - Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Adiyy narrated to us, from Ash'ath, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: I never prayed behind anyone after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) whose prayer was more complete and more brief than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2788","(2788) - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Ash'ath, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade prayer between graves."
"2789","(2789) - Muhammad ibn Bahr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Zayd al-Ammi narrated to us, from his father, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever walks to fulfill the need of his Muslim brother, Allah writes for him, for every step he takes, a good deed, until he returns from where he left him. If his need is fulfilled, he leaves his sins as on the day his mother bore him. And if he perishes in the course of it, O what a perishing one - he enters Paradise without reckoning."
"2790","(2790) - Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Shami al-Abbadani narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Nuh ibn Dhakwan, from his brother Ayyub, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of the Most Generous of the most generous? Allah is the Most Generous of the most generous, and I am the most generous of the children of Adam, and the most generous of them after me is a man who learned knowledge and spread his knowledge; he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection as a nation alone. And a man who was generous with his soul in the path of Allah until he is killed."
"2791","Abu Qilabah Abd Allah ibn Zayd al-Jarmi, from Anas. (2791) - Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abi Qilabah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to come to Umm Sulaym and take the midday rest at her place, and he would pray upon a leather mat and take rest, and he used to sweat profusely, so she would collect the sweat from the leather mat and put it in bottles of perfume. And he used to pray upon the khumrah (small straw mat)."
"2792","(2792) - Ibrahim narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abi Qilabah, from Anas, who said: Bilal was commanded to make the Adhan even and the Iqamah odd."
"2793","(2793) - Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha' - whose kunyah was Abu al-Manazil - narrated to us, from Abi Qilabah, from Anas, who said: Bilal was commanded to make the Adhan even and the Iqamah odd."
"2794","(2794) - Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abi Qilabah, from Anas, who said: He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Dhuhr in Madinah as four, and prayed at Dhu al-Hulayfah two rak'ahs, and I heard them shouting loudly with both: Hajj and Umrah."
"2795","(2795) - Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abi Qilabah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to come to Umm Sulaym and take the midday rest at her place, and he used to sweat profusely, so she would put it in bottles. And he used to pray upon the khumrah."
"2796","(2796) - Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abi Qilabah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When dinner is present and prayer is established, begin with dinner."
"2797","(2797) - Surayj narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abi Qilabah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When dinner is placed and prayer is established, begin with dinner."
"2798","(2798) - Abd Allah ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abi Qilabah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until people boast about mosques."
"2799","(2799) - Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abi Qilabah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said something similar."
"2800","(2800) - Ja'far ibn Mihran al-Sabbak narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abi Qilabah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you becomes drowsy while praying, let him leave until he understands what he is saying."
"2801","(2801) - Ishaq narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, who said: The book of Abi Qilabah was read to us, from Anas, who said: When one of you becomes drowsy, let him leave until he knows what he is doing."
"2802","(2802) - Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abi Qilabah, in marfu' form, he said: When one of you becomes drowsy in prayer, let him leave and sleep."
"2803","(2803) - Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abi Qilabah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When one of you becomes drowsy in his prayer, let him leave and lie down to sleep."
"2804","(2804) - Ja'far ibn Mihran narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abi Qilabah, from Anas, who said: Bilal was commanded to repeat the Adhan and to make the Iqamah single."
"2805","(2805) - Makhlad ibn Abi Zumayl narrated to me, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr al-Raqqi narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abi Qilabah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with his Companions, and when he finished his prayer he turned to them with his face and said: Do you recite in your prayer behind the imam while the imam is reciting? They fell silent. He said it three times. Then a speaker - or speakers - said: We do indeed do so. He said: Then do not do so; let one of you recite the Opening of the Book (al-Fatihah) to himself."
"2806","(2806) - Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abi Qilabah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to two horned black-and-white rams and slaughtered them with his hand."
"2807","(2807) - Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abi Qilabah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"2808","(2808) - Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah and Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, they said: Isma'il ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Khalid, from Abi Qilabah, who said: Anas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every nation has a trustworthy one, and our trustworthy one, O nation, is Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah."
"2809","(2809) - Ishaq narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abi Qilabah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in his house, and the servant boy of the Messenger of Allah, called Anjashah, was chanting. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to you, O Anjashah, gently, your driving with the glass vessels. Abu Qilabah said: Meaning women."
"2810","(2810) - Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Isma'il narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abi Qilabah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon his wives, with a driver driving them called Anjashah. So he said: Woe to you, O Anjashah, gently, your driving with the glass vessels. Abu Qilabah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke a word which, if some of you had spoken it, you would have blamed him for it."
"2811","(2811) - Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Isma'il narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abi Qilabah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Dhuhr in Madinah as four, and prayed Asr at Dhu al-Hulayfah as two."
"2812","(2812) - Ishaq narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abi Qilabah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Dhuhr in Madinah as four, and prayed Asr at Dhu al-Hulayfah as two."
"2813","(2813) - Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abi Qilabah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three, whoever has them finds through them the sweetness of faith: that Allah and His Messenger be more beloved to him than anything besides them, that he love a person and love him only for Allah, and that he hate to return to disbelief as he hates to be kindled a fire and then be cast into it."
"2814","(2814) - Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abi Qilabah, from Anas, who said: I was riding behind Abu Talhah, and they were shouting loudly with both: Hajj and Umrah."
"2815","(2815) - Abu Khaythamah and Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, they said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Hajjaj ibn Abi Uthman, Abu Raja', freedman of Abi Qilabah, narrated to me, from Abi Qilabah, who said: Anas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every nation has a trustworthy one, and our trustworthy one, O nation, is Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah."
"2816","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Hajjaj ibn Abi Uthman, Abu Raja the freed slave of Abu Qilabah narrated to me, from Abu Qilabah, who said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to me: A group from Ukl, eight men, came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and pledged allegiance to him upon Islam. They found the land unhealthy and their bodies fell sick, so they complained of that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Will you not go out with our herdsman among his camels and take of their urine and milk? So they recovered. Then they killed the herdsman and drove off the camels. That reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he sent men in pursuit of them. They were caught and brought to him, and he ordered concerning them: their hands and feet were cut off, their eyes were branded, then they were cast into the sun until they died."
"2817","Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Salih ibn Rustum narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: We went out with him to the sanctuary. The prayer came, so he said: Will you not dismount so we may pray? I said: If only you would go forward to this mosque. He said: Which mosque? It was said: The mosque of Banu so-and-so. He showed alarm and said: I heard him say (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): There will come upon my ummah a time when they will boast of mosques but will maintain them only a little."
"2818","Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas: A Jewish man killed an Ansari slave girl for her silver ornaments, then threw her into a well and crushed her head with stones. He was seized and brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who ordered that he be stoned, so he was stoned until he died."
"2819","Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated to us, Rayhan ibn Said narrated to us, from Abbad, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted a household of the Ansar to use ruqyah for venomous stings, and he permitted ruqyah for the evil eye and for the self (affliction)."
"2820","Ibrahim ibn Said narrated to us, Rayhan ibn Said narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Mansur, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Men from my ummah will meet Isa son of Maryam and will witness the battle against the Dajjal."
"2821","Abu Khaythamah and Jafar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, both saying: Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr in Madinah as four, and prayed Asr at Dhu al-Hulayfah as two, and spent the night there until morning. When he prayed Fajr he mounted his riding camel, and when his mount rose with him he glorified Allah and said Allahu Akbar until it stood straight with him on al-Bayda. Then he joined between them (Hajj and Umrah). When we arrived at Makkah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered them to exit ihram. When the Day of Tarwiyah came they entered ihram for Hajj. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed seven camels with his own hand while they were standing, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed two horned black-and-white rams. The wording is Zuhayr's."
"2822","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived at Makkah he ordered them to exit ihram except whoever had the sacrificial animal with him. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed seven camels while they were standing."
"2823","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, who said: Seven days (of wedding stay) for the virgin and three for the previously married woman. Indeed, if I were to say it is from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) I would be truthful, but it is a sunnah."
"2824","Muslim ibn Abi Muslim al-Jarmi narrated to us, Makhlad ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The first lian in Islam was that Sharik ibn Sahma was accused by Hilal ibn Umayyah regarding his wife. It was raised to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Hilal, four witnesses, otherwise a hadd punishment on your back. He said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah knows I am truthful, and Allah will surely send down what will clear my back of flogging. So Allah sent down the verse of lian: And those who accuse their wives and have no witnesses but themselves, to the end of the verse. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him and said: Bear witness by Allah that you are of the truthful in what you accused her of regarding zina. He bore witness to that four testimonies. Then he said to him on the fifth: And the curse of Allah upon you if you are of the liars in what you accused her of regarding zina. So he did it. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called her and said: Stand and bear witness by Allah that he is of the liars in what he accused you of regarding zina. She bore witness to that four testimonies. Then he said to her on the fifth: And the wrath of Allah upon you if he is of the truthful in what he accused you of regarding zina. So she spoke. Makhlad said: When it came to the fourth or fifth she fell silent for a moment until they thought she would confess. Then she said: I will not disgrace my people for the rest of the day. So she went ahead with her statement. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) separated between them and said: Watch: if she brings him curly-haired, thin-shanked, then he is Sharik ibn Sahma's; and if she brings him fair, straight-haired, with very white eyes, then he is Hilal ibn Umayyah's. She brought him dark, curly-haired, thin-shanked. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not for what was revealed about them in the Book of Allah, I and she would have had another matter."
"2825","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Anas: Hilal ibn Umayyah accused his wife with Sharik ibn Sahma. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Watch her: if she brings him fair, straight-haired, then he is Hilal ibn Umayyah's; and if she brings him dark-eyed, curly-haired, thin-shanked, then he is Sharik ibn Sahma's. She brought him dark-eyed, curly-haired, thin-shanked."
"2826","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever slaughtered before the prayer, let him repeat. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, this is a day in which meat is desired. He mentioned some need of his neighbors as though the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) believed him. He said: And I have a young goat that is dearer to me than two sheep of meat. He said: So he permitted him, and I do not know whether his permission reached anyone besides him or not. Then the people turned to a small flock of sheep and distributed it."
"2827","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahm al-Antaki narrated to us, saying: I heard Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrating from Hisham al-Qurdusi, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned the jamrah on the Day of Sacrifice, then ordered the camels and they were sacrificed, while the barber was sitting with him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) leveled his hair that day with his hand, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) grasped the right side of his head over his hair, then said to the barber: Shave. So he shaved. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that day distributed his hair among those of the people who were present, one hair and two hairs. Then he grasped with his hand the left side of his head over his hair, then said to the barber: Shave. So he shaved, and he called Abu Talhah al-Ansari and handed it to him."
"2828","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Anas, and Ayyub from Muhammad; Hammad said: I think it is from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came on the day of Khaybar and it was said to him: The donkeys have been eaten. So he ordered Abu Talhah to announce: Allah and His Messenger forbid you from the meat of domestic donkeys, for it is filth. They said: So the pots were overturned."
"2829","Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Ismail ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, who said: We asked Anas: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dye his hair? He said: He did not reach the need for dye; there were white hairs in his beard. He said: I said to him: Did Abu Bakr dye? He said: Yes, with henna and katam."
"2830","Amr ibn al-Dahhak narrated to us, my father narrated to us, saying: I heard Ashath al-Humrani, saying: Muhammad ibn Sirin said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to me that Abu Talhah heard that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had no food with him. So he went and hired himself for a sa of barley, working that day of his. He brought it and said: Bake this. She said: It is barley, but make it khatifah (a porridge). So she made it. He sent Anas ibn Malik and said: Go to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and speak to him privately between you and him. He came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while his companions were with him, and said: The food? He said: Yes. He said: Arise. So they arose. When Anas came to Abu Talhah, he said: I said this. He said: The food? I disliked lying. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arose and invited ten; they entered and ate until they were full. Then he invited ten; they entered and ate until they were full. Then he invited ten; they entered and ate until they were full. Then there remained for his family what would satisfy them."
"2831","Al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Ibn Sirin, who said: Anas was asked about the dyeing of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had only a little graying, but Abu Bakr and Umar dyed with henna and katam. He said: And Abu Bakr brought his father Abu Quhafah to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the conquest of Makkah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Bakr: If only you had left the old man in his house, we would have come to him out of honor for Abu Bakr. He said: He embraced Islam while his beard and head were like thaghamah (a white plant). He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Change it, and avoid black for him."
"2832","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, who said: I said to Anas: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say qunut in the Fajr prayer? He said: Yes, after bowing. He said: Then he was asked after that: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say qunut in the Fajr prayer? He said: Yes, briefly after bowing."
"2833","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Anas, who said: I bear witness that Allah is true, and that meeting Him is true, and that the Hour is true, and that Paradise is true, and Hell is true. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the trial of the Dajjal, and from the trial of life and death, and from the punishment of the grave and the punishment of Hell. Abu Khaythamah said: As though he meant the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2834","Sufyan ibn Waki narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Khalid, from Muhammad, who said: I asked Anas ibn Malik: Did Umar say qunut? He said: One better than Umar said qunut: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said qunut."
"2835","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah al-Wasiti narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Yunus, from Ibn Sirin, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped and gave the cupper his wage."
"2836","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Jabalah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Marwan narrated to us, from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to visit us and mix with us. There was a boy with us called Abu Umayr. He said: O Abu Umayr, what happened to the nughayr (a small bird)?"
"2837","Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Sahl ibn Hammad narrated to us, Hafs ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Kathir ibn Shinzhir narrated to us, from Ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seeking knowledge is an obligation upon every Muslim."
"2838","Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Muadh ibn Muadh narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad, from Anas, who said: We were forbidden that a town dweller sell for a Bedouin."
"2839","Musa ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, who said: Anas narrated little from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when he narrated he would say: Or as he said."
"2840","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Hafs narrated to us, from Hisham, from Muhammad, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned the jamarat while the barber was sitting. He ordered the sacrificial camels and they were sacrificed. He said to the barber: Here, gesturing with his hand to the right side. He said: He distributed his hair among those next to him. He said: Then he gestured to the barber toward his left side, so he shaved it, and he gave it to Umm Sulaym."
"2841","Ibrahim ibn Said narrated to us, Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Jarir ibn Hazim, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, who said: Anas said: The head of al-Husayn was brought to Ubaydullah ibn Ziyad in a basin, and he said something about his beauty. Anas said: He was the one among them who most resembled the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2842","Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Every prophet has a supplication he made and was answered, and I have withheld my supplication as intercession for my ummah."
"2843","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ubayy: Allah has commanded me to recite to you. He said: Did Allah name me to you? He said: Allah named you to me. So Ubayy began to weep."
"2844","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not wrong the believer a good deed; he is given provision for it in this world and rewarded for it in the Hereafter. As for the disbeliever, he is given for his good deeds until when he reaches the Hereafter there will be no good deed left for which he is given good."
"2845","Abu Nasr al-Tammar narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from knowledge that does not benefit, and a deed that is not raised, and a heart that does not humble itself, and a word that is not heard."
"2846","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You, and he mentioned the like of the hadith of Abu Nasr."
"2847","Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, saying: I said to Anas: How was the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: It was wavy hair, neither curly nor straight, between the earlobe and his shoulder."
"2848","Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath, Ibn Hisab, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj, and Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Tarjuman narrated to us, saying: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take suhur, for in suhur there is blessing."
"2849","Khalaf ibn Hisham and Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, both saying: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the son of Adam had two valleys of wealth, he would seek a third valley to add to them. Nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam but dust, and Allah turns to whoever repents."
"2850","Khalaf and Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, both saying: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Spittle in the mosque is a sin and its expiation is burying it."
"2851","Khalaf, Abd al-Wahid, and Ibn Hisab narrated to us, saying: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Muslim plants a plant or sows a crop and a bird, a human, or an animal eats from it but it is charity for him."
"2852","Khalaf and Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, both saying: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the lightest of people in prayer while completing it."
"2853","Kamil ibn Talhah al-Jahdari narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be balanced in prostration, and let none of you spread his forearms as the dog spreads them."
"2854","Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever forgets a prayer, let him pray it when he remembers it."
"2855","Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated to us with his isnad the like of it."
"2856","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Said informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), something similar."
"2857","Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever forgets a prayer, let him pray it when he remembers it; there is no expiation for it but that."
"2858","Abd al-Wahid and Ibn Hisab narrated to us, both saying: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The son of Adam grows old while two things of his stay young: greed for wealth and greed for long life."
"2859","Abd al-Wahid and Ibn Hisab narrated to us, both saying: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: If the son of Adam had two valleys of wealth he would seek a third valley to add to them. Nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam but dust, and Allah turns to whoever repents."
"2860","Hudbah narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slaughtered his sacrifice with his own hand and said takbir over it."
"2861","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is more joyful at the repentance of His servant than one of you who wakes to find his camel, which he had lost in a desolate land."
"2862","Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah, Thabit, and Humayd, from Anas, who said: Prices rose in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They said: O Messenger of Allah, set prices for us. He said: Allah is the Withholder, the Extender, the Pricer, the Provider. I hope to meet Allah while none of you seeks me for an injustice in a life or wealth."
"2863","Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pass by a date and nothing would prevent him from taking it except fear that it might be charity."
"2864","Shayban narrated to us, Abu Hilal narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never addressed us but he said: There is no faith for one who has no trustworthiness, and no religion for one who has no covenant."
"2865","Shayban narrated to us, Abu Hilal narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among the briefest of people in prayer while completing it."
"2866","Shayban narrated to us, Abu Hilal narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The servant remains in good so long as he does not hasten. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how does he hasten? He said: He says: I supplicated and I do not see it answered for me."
"2867","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah informed us, from Anas: A slave girl was found with her head crushed between two stones. She was asked: Who did this to you? So-and-so? So-and-so? Until a Jew was mentioned, so she nodded with her head. The Jew was seized, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that his head be crushed with stones."
"2868","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah informed us, from Anas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking while standing."
"2869","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a camel driver called Anjashah, and he had a beautiful voice. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Gently, O Anjashah, do not break the glass vessels. Qatadah said: Meaning the weak women."
"2870","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed a man driving a sacrificial camel and said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial animal. He said: Ride it, woe to you."
"2871","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no contagion and no bad omen, but I like the good omen: the good word, the pleasant word."
"2872","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, saying: I said to Anas: Was handshaking practiced in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes. Qatadah said: And al-Hasan used to shake hands."
"2873","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, that Anas informed him: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed four umrahs, all of them in Dhu al-Qadah except the one with his Hajj: his umrah from al-Hudaybiyah or at the time of al-Hudaybiyah in Dhu al-Qadah, his umrah of the following year in Dhu al-Qadah, his umrah from al-Jiranah where he distributed the spoils of Hunayn in Dhu al-Qadah, and his umrah with his Hajj."
"2874","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, saying: I said to Anas: Which clothing was most beloved to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or most pleasing to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: The hibarah (a Yemeni striped garment)."
"2875","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasted continuously (wisal), so the people fasted continuously. He forbade them from wisal and said: I am fed, if Allah wills, and given drink."
"2876","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, or from a man, from Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had large palms, large feet, and a handsome face; I never saw anyone like him after him (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2877","Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While I was traveling in Paradise, I came upon a river whose banks were domes of hollow pearls. I said: What is this, O Jibril? He said: This is al-Kawthar which your Lord gave you. The angel struck with his hand, and its clay was pungent musk."
"2878","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed two black-and-white horned rams, placed his foot on their sides, slaughtered them with his hand, and said the tasmiyah and takbir."
"2879","Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, saying: We said to Anas: Who compiled the Quran in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Four, all of them from the Ansar: Ubayy ibn Kab, Muadh ibn Jabal, Zayd ibn Thabit, and a man of the Ansar called Abu Zayd."
"2880","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah informed us, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one of the people of Paradise wishes to return to this world even if he had ten times its like, except the martyr, for he wishes he would return to this world and be killed ten times for what he sees of merit."
"2881","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas: Al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf complained to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about lice, so he permitted them to wear silk shirts. I saw each of them wearing a silk shirt."
"2882","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, and Umar used to begin the recitation with: All praise is due to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"2883","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas: A group from Uraynah came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, we found Madinah unhealthy; our bellies swelled and our flesh wasted. So he ordered them, and they went to the herdsman of the sadaqah camels and drank of their milk and urine until their bodies recovered. Then they killed the herdsman, drove off the camels, and apostatized. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent men in pursuit of them, so they were brought. He cut off their hands and feet, branded their eyes, and cast them into the lava field."
"2884","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: A tailor in Madinah invited the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to barley bread and melted fat in which there was pumpkin. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked pumpkin, so I used to serve it before him. Anas said: Pumpkin has pleased me ever since."
"2885","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas and al-Hasan: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you spit to his right; let him spit to his left."
"2886","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Spittle in the mosque is a sin and its expiation is burying it."
"2887","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will come out of the Fire after it has touched them with scorching. They will enter Paradise, and the people of Paradise will call them the Jahannamis (people of Hell)."
"2888","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant believes until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself of good."
"2889","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: A man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): A man loves a people but has not joined them? He said: A person is with whom he loves."
"2890","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Anas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will come out of the Fire whoever says: There is no god but Allah, and there was in his heart good weighing a barley grain. Then he said: There will come out of the Fire whoever says: There is no god but Allah, and there was in his heart good weighing a wheat grain. Then there will come out of the Fire whoever says: There is no god but Allah, and there was in his heart good weighing an atom."
"2891","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, who said: We used to visit Anas while his baker was standing. He said: Eat, for I do not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ever saw a thin loaf, nor a roasted whole sheep with his own eyes, until he met Allah the Mighty and Majestic."
"2892","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade steeping dates and raisins together."
"2893","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, that he said one day: I will narrate to you a hadith that no one after me will narrate to you; I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Hour will not come, or he said: Among the signs of the Hour are that knowledge will be lifted, ignorance will appear, wine will be drunk, zina will appear, men will decrease and women will increase, until there will be one caretaker for fifty women."
"2894","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, saying: I asked Anas: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dye his hair? He said: He did not reach that; his graying was only at his temples, but Abu Bakr and Umar dyed with henna and katam."
"2895","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik: A man who had become drunk was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He ordered about twenty men, and they beat him with palm stalks and sandals. Then a drunk man was brought to Abu Bakr and he flogged him forty. When Umar took charge and people persisted in wine, he consulted the people. Abd al-Rahman said: I think you should make it ... and a word was cut off from Abu Yala; I think he said: eighty."
"2896","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, who said: I witnessed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with his companions at al-Zawra, or he said: at the houses of Madinah. He wanted to perform ablution, so a small cup with a little water was brought. He placed his hand on the cup, and water began to gush from between his fingers until all the people performed ablution. I said to Anas: How many were you? He said: About three hundred."
"2897","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas: Umm Sulaym sent with him something; Hammam named in it fresh dates, to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He would take a handful and send it to one of his wives, and take a handful while he desired it himself."
"2898","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from leprosy, elephantiasis, madness, and evil diseases."
"2899","Nafi ibn Khalid al-Tahi narrated to us, Nuh ibn Qays narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Qays, from Qatadah, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Death will be brought on the Day of Resurrection like a black-and-white ram. It will be made to stand between Paradise and Hell. Then a caller will call: O people of Paradise? They will say: At Your service, our Lord. He said: It will be said: Do you recognize this? They will say: Yes, our Lord, this is death. It will be slaughtered as the sheep is slaughtered. These will be secure, and the hope of these will be cut off."
"2900","Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Hisab narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah will gather people on the Day of Resurrection, and they will be inspired likewise, saying: If only we would intercede with our Lord so He relieves us from this place of ours. He said: They will come to Adam and say: O Adam, father of mankind, Allah created you with His hand and made His angels prostrate to you; intercede for us with your Lord so He relieves us from our place. He will say: I am not for that, and he will mention the sin he committed and feel shy before his Lord because of it. Rather go to Nuh, the first messenger Allah sent. So they will come to Nuh, and he will say: I am not for that, and he will mention the sin he committed and feel shy before his Lord. Rather go to Ibrahim. He said: They will come to Ibrahim, and he will say: I am not for that, and he will mention the sin he committed and feel shy before his Lord because of it. Rather go to Musa. So they will come to Musa, and he will say: I am not for that, and he will mention the sin he committed and feel shy before his Lord because of it. Rather go to Isa, the Spirit of Allah and His Word. He said: They will come to Isa, and he will say: I am not for that, but go to Muhammad, a servant whom Allah has forgiven his past and future sins. He said: They will come to me, and I will seek permission and it will be granted to me. When I see my Lord I will fall prostrate. He will leave me as long as Allah wills to leave me. Then He will say: Rise, O Muhammad; speak and you will be heard, ask and you will be given, intercede and your intercession will be accepted. I will raise my head and praise my Lord with praises He teaches me. Then I will intercede, and a limit will be set for me, and I will bring them out of the Fire and admit them into Paradise. Then I will return and fall prostrate, and praise my Lord with praises He teaches me. Then I will intercede, and a limit will be set for me, and I will bring them out of the Fire and admit them into Paradise. Then I will return and fall prostrate, and praise my Lord with praises He teaches me. Then it will be said: O Muhammad, speak and you will be heard, ask and you will be given, intercede and your intercession will be accepted. I will raise my head and praise my Lord with praises He teaches me. Then I will intercede, and a limit will be set for me, and I will bring them out of the Fire and admit them into Paradise. He said regarding the third or fourth: None will remain in the Fire but whom the Quran has held back. Qatadah said: That is, eternal stay became due."
"2901","Abdullah ibn Awn al-Kharraz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, from Misar ibn Kidam, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood (in prayer) until his feet or shanks swelled. It was said to him: Has Allah not forgiven you your past and future sins? He said: Should I not be a grateful servant?"
"2902","Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, al-Qasim narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until knowledge is lifted, ignorance appears, women increase and men decrease, until a single man will be caretaker of fifty women."
"2903","Surayj narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, one of our companions informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lifespan of my ummah is between sixty and seventy, and the fewest of them are those who reach eighty."
"2904","Surayj narrated to us, Abu Hafs al-Abbar narrated to us, from a man of the people of Sham, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seeking knowledge is an obligation upon every Muslim."
"2905","Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Basri narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from al-Muthanna ibn Said, from Qatadah, from Anas: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went on campaign, he would say: O Allah, You are my support and You are my helper, and by You I fight."
"2906","Musa ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from al-Muthanna, from Qatadah, from Anas: When a strong wind blew, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say: O Allah, I ask You of the good of what it was commanded with, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of what it was commanded with."
"2907","Musa narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Jarir ibn Hazim, from Qatadah, saying: I asked Anas ibn Malik: How was the recitation of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: He used to prolong his voice with prolongation."
"2908","Musa narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: When Musa, the prophet of Allah, called his companion to the term that was between them, his companion said to him: Every sheep that gives birth unlike its color, its offspring is yours. He said: He set stakes at the water. When they saw the stakes they were frightened and rushed about, and all of them gave birth to spotted lambs except one sheep. So he took their offspring that year."
"2909","Khallad ibn Aslam narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Khaybar, he said: When we descend into the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of those warned."
"2910","Al-Qawariri and Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us, both saying: Harami ibn Umarah narrated to us, from Shubah, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire. In the hadith of Musa there is no deliberately."
"2911","Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on Uhud with Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman. It shook with them, so he struck it with his foot and said: Be firm, O Uhud! A prophet, a siddiq, and two martyrs."
"2912","Ibrahim ibn Ararah al-Sami narrated to us, Muslim ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Umar ibn Nabhan narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate with the insides of his palms, saying: Thus, showing his palms."
"2913","Ibrahim narrated to us, Muslim ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Umar ibn Nabhan narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray in his khuffs and sandals."
"2914","Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Abdullah al-Tahhan narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fasting five days of the year: the day of Fitr, the day of Sacrifice, and the three days of Tashriq."
"2915","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: The prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated when he was taken up to heaven. He said: I came upon Idris in the fourth heaven."
"2916","Abd al-Rahman ibn Sallam narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Qatadah, Thabit, and Humayd narrated to us, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading them in prayer when a man came and joined the prayer while out of breath. He said: Allahu Akbar, praise be to Allah, much, good, blessed praise. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his prayer, he said: Which of you spoke the words? The people fell silent. He said: Which of you spoke the words? He said no harm. The man said: I did, O Messenger of Allah; I came while out of breath and said them. He said: I saw twelve angels racing to it, which of them would raise it."
"2917","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abdah narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the People of the Book greet you, say: And upon you."
"2918","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr al-Abdi narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let not the adhan of Bilal prevent you from suhur, for there is something in his sight."
"2919","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: What is with people who raise their eyes to the sky in their prayer? His speech about that was severe, until he said: They will stop that, or their sights will be snatched away."
"2920","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Shubah, from Qatadah, from Anas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw meat and said: What is this? They said: It was given in charity to Barirah. He said: It is charity for her, and a gift for us."
"2921","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Anas: Umm Sulaym asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a woman who sees in her dream what a man sees. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the woman sees that fluid and ejaculates, ghusl is upon her. Umm Sulaym said: O Messenger of Allah, can this be? He said: Yes. The fluid of the man is thick and white, and the fluid of the woman is thin and yellow; whichever precedes or dominates, the child resembles it."
"2922","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik: Usayyah, Dhakwan, and Banu Lihyan came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and sought his aid, having embraced Islam, against their enemy. He aided them with seventy of the Ansar called the reciters. They gathered firewood by day and prayed by night, until when they were at Bir Maunah they killed them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said qunut for a month supplicating against them."
"2923","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, from Ali ibn Masadah, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All the children of Adam err, and the best of those who err are the repentant."
"2924","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, from Ali ibn Masadah, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Islam is open, and faith is in the heart, then he gestured with his hand to his chest: Taqwa is here, taqwa is here."
"2925","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Harami narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked pumpkin. He said: I saw him one day eating food containing pumpkin, and I would bring it close to him."
"2926","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Harami ibn Umarah narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was sent, I and the Hour, like these two. Abu Said said with his two fingers: the index and the middle."
"2927","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, Anas narrated to us: The prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It will be said to a man on the Day of Resurrection: What do you think, if you had the earth full of gold, would you ransom yourself with it? He will say: Yes. He said: It will be said to him: You were asked for easier than that."
"2928","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham and Abu Amir al-Aqadi both narrated to us, both saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will come out of the Fire whoever says: There is no god but Allah, and there was in his heart good weighing a wheat grain. Then there will come out of the Fire whoever says: There is no god but Allah, and there was in his heart what weighs an atom."
"2929","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Harami ibn Umarah narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every prophet has a supplication he made, and I have stored my supplication as intercession for my ummah on the Day of Resurrection."
"2930","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Harami ibn Umarah narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The moon split in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2931","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Shubah, from Qatadah, from Anas, regarding His saying: The Hour has drawn near and the moon has split. He said: It split in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2932","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Abd al-Ala narrated to us, saying: Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: Shall I not narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He says: Among the signs of the Hour are that knowledge will be lifted, ignorance will appear, wine will be drunk, zina will spread, men will decrease and women will increase, until there will be one caretaker for fifty women."
"2933","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us; Said said: Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik: This verse was revealed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Indeed We have granted you a clear victory, upon his return from al-Hudaybiyah. It was revealed while his companions were filled with grief, kept from their rites, and they sacrificed the sacrificial animals at al-Hudaybiyah. When this verse was revealed, he said to his companions: A verse better than the whole world has been revealed to me. When the prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited it, a man of the people said: Congratulations, O prophet of Allah; Allah has made clear to us what He will do with you, so what will He do with us? Then Allah revealed after it: That He may admit the believing men and believing women into gardens beneath which rivers flow."
"2934","Huraym ibn Abd al-Ala Abu Hamzah al-Asadi narrated to us, al-Mutamir narrated to us, saying: I heard my father narrating from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The generality of the bequest of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when death came to him was: Prayer, and what your right hands possess, until he kept repeating it in his chest and his tongue could no longer utter it clearly."
"2935","Abu Hamzah Huraym narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, from his father, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to say: I repent in a day seventy times."
"2936","Muhammad ibn al-Minhal al-Darir narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not raise his hands in any supplication except in istisqa; he would raise his hands until the whiteness of his armpits was seen."
"2937","Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ubaydullah Abu Ayyub al-Raqqi narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Amr al-Raqqi narrated to us, from Mamar, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to put on sandals while standing."
"2938","Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath and Said ibn Abi al-Rabi, and this is the wording of Abd al-Wahid, both narrated to us, saying: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: Three men set out seeking provisions for their families when rain overtook them. An overhanging rock fell upon them so that they could see no opening from it. One of them said: The rock has fallen and the trace is effaced, and none knows your place but Allah; supplicate Allah by your most reliable deeds. He said: A man said: O Allah, You know I had two parents; I used to milk for them in their vessel. When I found them sleeping I would stand over their heads until they woke, whenever they woke, disliking to disturb their drowsiness in their heads. O Allah, if You know I did that only hoping for Your mercy and fearing Your punishment, relieve us. He said: A third of the rock moved. The second said: O Allah, if You know that a woman pleased me, and he offered her a reward; when he gained power over her he gave her in full her reward and left her to herself. O Allah, if You know I did that only hoping for Your mercy and fearing Your punishment, relieve us. He said: A third of the rock moved. The other said: O Allah, You know I hired a worker for work he would do for me. He came seeking his wage while I was angry, so I rebuked him; he went and left his wage. I collected it for him and invested it until all this wealth came from it. He came to me seeking his wage, so I gave him all of that. Had I wished I would have given him only his first wage. O Allah, if You know I did that hoping for Your mercy and fearing Your punishment, relieve us. He said: The rock moved and they walked out."
"2939","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Three men of those before you among people, and he mentioned something similar or close to it."
"2940","Nasr ibn Ali al-Jahdami narrated to us, Nuh ibn Qays narrated to us, from his brother Khalid ibn Qays, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, how many prayers has Allah obligated upon His servants? He said: Five prayers. He said: Is there anything before or after them? He said: Allah has obligated upon His servants five prayers. The man swore by Allah he would neither add to them nor decrease. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If he is truthful he will enter Paradise."
"2941","Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: A speaker said: O prophet of Allah, does he not intend Madinah? Meaning the Dajjal. He said: He will head toward it and find the angels at its passes and gates guarding it from the Dajjal."
"2942","Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Muadh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: The prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to go around his wives in one hour of the night and day, and they were eleven. He said: I said to Anas: Could he manage that? He said: We used to say he had the strength of thirty."
"2943","Abu Yusuf al-Jizi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Walid al-Adani narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mamar, from Qatadah, from Anas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to go around his wives with a single bath; meaning he went around his wives in one night and bathed once."
"2944","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Look whom you see in the mosque. I looked, and there was Zayd ibn Thabit. I called him, and we ate dates and drank water. Then we went out to prayer and the prayer was established."
"2945","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to me, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, saying: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to me that he heard Qatadah ibn Diamah; Anas ibn Malik narrated to us: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) having performed ablution but left on his foot a spot the size of a fingernail. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Return and perfect your ablution."
"2946","Al-Harith ibn Miskin narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Jarir ibn Hazim, from Qatadah, from Anas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered aqiqah for al-Hasan and al-Husayn with two rams."
"2947","Ubaydullah ibn Muadh narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, saying: When Musa, the prophet of Allah, called his companion to the term that was between them, his companion said to him: Every sheep that gives birth unlike its color, its offspring is yours. He said: He set stakes at the water. When they saw the stakes they were frightened and rushed about, and all of them gave birth to spotted lambs except one sheep. He said: So he took their offspring that year."
"2948","Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, Nuh ibn Qays narrated to us, from his brother Khalid ibn Qays, from Qatadah, from Anas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to Bakr ibn Wail: From Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, to Bakr ibn Wail: Embrace Islam and you will be safe. We found none to read it except a man of Banu Dubayah, so they are called Banu al-Katib (the sons of the scribe)."
"2949","Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, my father informed us, Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Uhud is a mountain that loves us and we love it."
"2950","Nasr narrated to us, my father informed me, from al-Muthanna ibn Said, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went on campaign, he would say: O Allah, You are my support and You are my helper, and by You I fight."
"2951","Ubaydullah ibn Muadh al-Anbari narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you believes until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself."
"2952","Ubaydullah ibn Umar ibn Maysarah narrated to us, Harami ibn Umarah narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the son of Adam had a valley of wealth he would seek a second to add to it. If he had a second he would seek a third to add to it. Nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam but dust, and Allah turns to whoever repents."
"2953","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Aruzzi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: A man used to trade in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and was weak in judgment. His family came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, place him under interdiction, for he trades while weak in judgment. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him and forbade him from selling. He said: O prophet of Allah, I cannot bear to leave selling. He said (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): If you will not leave selling, say: Take, no cheating."
"2954","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Aruzzi narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, Said informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The two tribes of the Ansar, Aws and Khazraj, boasted. Aws said: Of us is the one washed by angels, Hanzalah ibn al-Rahib; of us is the one for whom the Throne of the Merciful shook, Sad ibn Muadh; of us is the one protected by wasps, Asim ibn Thabit ibn Abi al-Aqlah; and of us is the one whose testimony was accepted as that of two men, Khuzaymah ibn Thabit. The Khazrajis said: Of us are four who compiled the Quran in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), whom none besides them compiled: Zayd ibn Thabit, Abu Zayd, Ubayy ibn Kab, and Muadh ibn Jabal."
"2955","Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, Nuh ibn Qays narrated to us, from his brother Khalid ibn Qays, from Qatadah, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to Khosrow and Caesar and to every tyrant, calling them to Allah."
"2956","Muhammad ibn al-Minhal al-Darir narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Said and Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will come out of the Fire whoever says: There is no god but Allah, and there was in his heart good weighing a barley grain. Then there will come out of the Fire whoever says: There is no god but Allah, and there was in his heart good weighing a wheat grain. Then there will come out of the Fire whoever says: There is no god but Allah, and there was in his heart good weighing an atom."
"2957","Yazid said: I met Shubah and narrated this hadith to him. Shubah said: Qatadah narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the hadith, except that Shubah put in place of the atom a durah (maize grain). He said: Abu Bistam misread in it."
"2958","He said: Yazid narrated to us; then I met Imran al-Qattan Abu al-Awwam and narrated the hadith to him. Imran said: Qatadah narrated to me, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the hadith. Yazid said: Imran erred and was mistaken in it. Yazid said: Imran was a Haruri; he held the sword against the people of the qiblah. When Ibrahim went out to Basra seeking the caliphate, he put him in charge of the kharaj of the Euphrates. He said: Ibrahim consulted him about something, and Imran gave him a fatwa; Ibrahim gave fatwa to men accordingly; Imran says: They were all killed."
"2959","Salih ibn Hatim ibn Wardan and others narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not raise his hands in any supplication except in istisqa; he would raise his hands until the whiteness of his armpits was seen."
"2960","Abu Yasir al-Mustamli narrated to us, Suwayd Abu Hatim al-Jahdari narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a flea bit a man and he cursed it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not curse it, for it awakened a prophet among the prophets for prayer."
"2961","Shabab ibn Khayyat narrated to us, Durust ibn Hamzah narrated to us, Matar al-Warraq narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There are no two servants who love each other for Allah, one of them meets his companion and shakes his hand, and they send blessings upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except that they do not separate until their sins are forgiven, past and future."
"2962","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the signs of the Hour are that knowledge will be taken away and ignorance will appear."
"2963","Al-Hasan ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Shubah, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: There was an alarm in Madinah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rode a horse belonging to Abu Talhah called Mandub, and said: We saw no alarm, and indeed we found him to be a swift sea."
"2964","Suwayd ibn Said narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be in my ummah division and sects who speak good words but do evil deeds; they recite the Quran but it does not pass their throats; one of you will belittle his prayer compared to their prayer and his fasting compared to their fasting; they are the worst of creation; glad tidings to whoever kills them and whom they kill; they call to the Book of Allah but have nothing to do with it; whoever kills them is closer to Allah than they are. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is their mark? He said: Shaving the head."
"2965","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Arubah, Qatadah narrated to us, that Anas ibn Malik narrated to them that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) climbed Uhud, followed by Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman, and it trembled beneath them, so he said: Be still: a Prophet, a truthful one, and two martyrs."
"2966","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is wrong with people who raise their eyes to the sky, and he spoke severely about that, and said: Let them stop doing that, or their sight will be snatched away."
"2967","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not raise his hands in any supplication except in the prayer for rain, for he would raise his hands until the whiteness of his armpits was seen."
"2968","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Husayn al-Muallim, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, no servant believes until he loves for his neighbor, or for his brother, what he loves for himself."
"2969","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is in his prayer, he is conversing privately with his Lord, so let him not spit in front of him nor to his right, but to his left under his foot."
"2970","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, he said: There was an alarm in Madinah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rode a horse belonging to Abu Talhah, and said: We saw nothing, and indeed we found him to be a swift sea."
"2971","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Every Prophet has a supplication with which he supplicated for his ummah, and I have kept my supplication hidden as intercession for my ummah."
"2972","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Complete the bowing and prostration, for by Allah, I see you from behind my back."
"2973","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not fast continuously. They said: But you fast continuously. He said: I am not like any of you; I am fed and given drink."
"2974","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking while standing."
"2975","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to sacrifice two white horned rams, placing his foot on their sides, slaughtering them with his own hand, naming Allah and saying takbir."
"2976","Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Muadh narrated to us, from his father, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) found a date and said: Were it not that I fear it is charity, I would have eaten it."
"2977","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It will be said to the disbeliever on the Day of Resurrection: If you had the world in gold, would you ransom yourself with it? He will say: Yes. Then it will be said: You were asked for something easier than that."
"2978","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says there is no god but Allah with good in his heart weighing a barley grain will come out of the Fire; then whoever says there is no god but Allah with good in his heart weighing a wheat grain will come out of the Fire; then whoever says there is no god but Allah with good in his heart weighing an atom will come out of the Fire."
"2979","Zuhayr narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Some people will be struck by blackening from the Fire as punishment for sins they committed, then Allah will admit them to Paradise by His grace and mercy and the intercession of the intercessors; they will be called the Jahannamis."
"2980","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The son of Adam grows old while two things stay young in him: greed for wealth and greed for life."
"2981","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, and Umar used to begin with All praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"2982","Abu Musa narrated to us, Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, and Umar used to begin with All praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"2983","Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muadh ibn Muadh narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"2984","Abu Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said al-Qattan narrated to us, from Hisham, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman, and he mentioned the like of it."
"2985","Abu Musa narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, the like of it, except that he said in his hadith: and perhaps he doubted about Anas."
"2986","Abu Musa narrated to us, Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman, and he mentioned the like of it, but he did not mention the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2987","Abu Musa narrated to us, Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be balanced in prostration, and let none of you spread his forearms like a dog."
"2988","Abu Musa narrated to us, Ibn Abi Adi and Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not raise his hands in any supplication except in the prayer for rain, until the whiteness of his armpits was seen; except that Abd al-Ala said: until the whiteness of his armpits, or the whiteness of his armpit, was seen."
"2989","Abu Musa narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, that Anas ibn Malik narrated to them from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) something similar."
"2990","Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam al-Ijli narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrate from Qatadah, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I repent in a day seventy times."
"2991","Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The general bequest of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when death came to him was prayer and what your right hands possess, until he kept repeating it with a gurgle in his chest while his tongue could not utter it fully."
"2992","Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrate from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: In Paradise there is a tree under whose shade a rider travels and does not cross it."
"2993","Musa ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Umar ibn Said al-Abahh narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: I served the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for ten years; he never said for something I did: Why did you do it? Nor for something I did not do: Why did you not do it?"
"2994","Musa ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Umar ibn Said al-Abahh narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says there is no god but Allah with good in his heart weighing a barley grain will come out of the Fire; and whoever says there is no god but Allah with good in his heart weighing a wheat grain will come out of the Fire; and whoever says there is no god but Allah with good in his heart weighing an atom will come out of the Fire. He said: It was said to Said: O Abu al-Nadr, do they come out after having been admitted? He said: Are you not Arabs? Can there be an exit except after an entrance?"
"2995","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah narrate from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Ansar are my inner circle and my trust; people will increase and they will decrease, so accept from their good-doers and pardon their wrong-doers."
"2996","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah narrate from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ubayy ibn Kab: Allah has commanded me to recite to you: Those who disbelieved. He said: And did He name me? He said: Yes. He said: Then he wept."
"2997","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah narrate from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If it were not that you would stop burying one another, I would have asked Allah to let you hear the punishment of the grave."
"2998","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: And I heard Qatadah narrate from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Straighten your rows, for straightening the rows is part of completing the prayer."
"2999","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, and I heard Qatadah narrate from Anas, that there was an alarm in Madinah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) borrowed a horse called Mandub, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We saw no alarm, and indeed we found him to be a swift sea."
"3000","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: And I heard Qatadah narrate from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was sent, I and the Hour, like these two. Shubah said: I heard Qatadah say: Like the superiority of one of them over the other; and I do not know whether he mentioned it from Anas or said it from Qatadah."
